<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.6">
  <book code="1SA" style="id">- Tov Rose New Messianic Version Bible</book>
  <para style="h">1 Samuel</para>
  <para style="mt">1 Samuel</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now there was a certain man of Ramatayim-Tzofim <char style="add">[double height of the watchers]</char>, of mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, and his name <char style="add">[was]</char> Elkanah <char style="add">[God Has Taken Possession]</char>, the son of Yerocham <char style="add">[showing pity]</char>, the son of Elihu <char style="add">[He is my God]</char>, the son of Tochu <char style="add">[lowly]</char>, the son of Tzuf <char style="add">[honeycomb]</char>, an Efrat [ashiness: fruitfulness]:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he had two wives; the name of the one <char style="add">[was]</char> Hannah <char style="add">[grace]</char>, and the name of the other P’ninah <char style="add">[jewel]</char>: and P’ninah <char style="add">[jewel]</char> had children, but Hannah <char style="add">[grace]</char> had no children.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And this man went up out of his city yearly to worship and to sacrifice unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> in Shiloh <char style="add">[Place of Rest]</char>. And the two sons of ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char>, Hofni <char style="add">[fighter]</char> and Pinchas <char style="add">[mouth of brass]</char>, the priests of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[were]</char> there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And when the time was that Elkanah <char style="add">[God Has Taken Possession]</char> offered, he gave to P’ninah <char style="add">[jewel]</char> his wife, and to all her sons and her daughters, portions:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />But unto Hannah <char style="add">[grace]</char> he gave a double portion; for he loved Hannah <char style="add">[grace]</char>: but the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had shut up her womb.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And her adversary also provoked her sore, for to make her be troubled <char style="pn">(be grieved; be displeased)</char>, because the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had shut up her womb.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And <char style="add">[as]</char> he did so year by year, when she went up to the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, so she provoked her; therefore she wept, and did not eat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then said Elkanah <char style="add">[God Has Taken Possession]</char> her husband to her, Hannah <char style="add">[grace]</char>, why weep you<char style="ord">i</char>? and why eat you<char style="ord">i</char> not? and why is you<char style="ord">i</char> heart grieved? <char style="add">[am]</char> not I better to you<char style="ord">i</char> than ten sons?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />So Hannah <char style="add">[grace]</char> rose up after they had eaten in Shiloh <char style="add">[Place of Rest]</char>, and after they had drunk. Now ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char> the priest sat upon a seat by a post of the temple of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And she <char style="add">[was]</char> in bitterness of soul, and prayed unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and wept sore.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And she vowed a vow, and said, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, if you<char style="ord">i</char> will indeed look on the affliction of you<char style="ord">i</char> female servant, and remember me, and not forget you<char style="ord">i</char> female servant, but will give unto you<char style="ord">i</char> female servant a man child, then I will give him unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> all the days of his life, and there shall no razor come upon his head.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And it came to pass, as she continued praying before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char> marked her mouth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Now Hannah <char style="add">[grace]</char>, she spoke in her heart; only her lips moved, but her voice was not heard: therefore ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char> thought she had been drunken.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char> said unto her, How long will you<char style="ord">i</char> be drunken? put away you<char style="ord">i</char> wine from you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Hannah <char style="add">[grace]</char> answered and said, No, my lord, I <char style="add">[am]</char> a woman of a sorrowful spirit: I have drunk neither wine nor strong drink, but have poured out my soul before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Count not you<char style="ord">i</char> female servant for a daughter of Belial <char style="add">[Worthless, Good for Nothing]</char>: for out of the abundance of my complaint and grief have I spoken up to this time.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Then ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char> answered and said, Go in peace: and the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> grant <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> petition that you<char style="ord">i</char> have asked of him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And she said, Let your<char style="ord">i</char> female servant find grace in your<char style="ord">i</char> sight. So the woman went her way, and did eat, and her Countenance <char style="pn">(Face, appearance; show favor)</char> was no more <char style="add">[sad]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And they rose up in the morning early, and worshipped before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and returned, and came to their house to Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>: and Elkanah <char style="add">[God Has Taken Possession]</char> knew Hannah <char style="add">[grace]</char> his wife; and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> remembered her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />For what reason it came to pass, when the time was come about after Hannah <char style="add">[grace]</char> had conceived, that she bore a son, and called his name Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, <char style="add">[saying]</char>, Because I have asked him of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the man Elkanah <char style="add">[God Has Taken Possession]</char>, and all his house, went up to offer unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> the yearly sacrifice, and his vow.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />But Hannah <char style="add">[grace]</char> went not up; for she said unto her husband, <char style="add">[I will not go up]</char> until the child be weaned, and <char style="add">[then]</char> I will bring him, that he may appear before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and there abide forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And Elkanah <char style="add">[God Has Taken Possession]</char> her husband said unto her, Do what seems you<char style="ord">i</char> good; wait until you<char style="ord">i</char> have weaned him; only the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> establish his word. So the woman abode, and gave her son suck until she weaned him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And when she had weaned him, she took him up with her, with three bullocks, and one eifah of flour, and a bottle of wine, and brought him unto the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in Shiloh <char style="add">[Place of Rest]</char>: and the child <char style="add">[was]</char> young.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And they killed a bullock, and brought the child to ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And she said, Oh my lord, <char style="add">[as]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> soul lives, my lord, I <char style="add">[am]</char> the woman that stood by you<char style="ord">i</char> here, praying unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />For this child I prayed; and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has given me my petition which I asked of him:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Therefore also I have lent him to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; as long as he lives he shall be lent to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And he worshipped the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> there.</para>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Hannah <char style="add">[grace]</char> prayed, and said, My heart rejoices in the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, my horn is exalted in the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: my mouth is enlarged over my enemies; because I rejoice in you<char style="ord">i</char> salvation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[There is]</char> none holy as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: for <char style="add">[there is]</char> none beside you<char style="ord">i</char>: neither <char style="add">[is there]</char> any rock like our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Talk no more so exceeding proudly; let <char style="add">[not]</char> arrogancy come out of your mouth: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> a God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of knowledge, and by him actions are weighed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />The bows of the mighty men <char style="add">[are]</char> broken, and they that stumbled are girded with strength.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[They that were]</char> full have hired out themselves for bread; and <char style="add">[they that were]</char> hungry ceased: so that the barren has born seven; and she that has many children is waxed feeble.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> kills, and makes alive: he brings down to the grave, and brings up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> makes poor, and makes rich: he brings low, and lifts up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />He raises up the poor out of the dust, <char style="add">[and]</char> lifts up the beggar from the dunghill, to set <char style="add">[them]</char> among princes, and to make them inherit the throne of glory: for the pillars of the earth <char style="add">[are]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char>, and he has set the world upon them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />He will keep the feet of his saints, and the wicked shall be silent in darkness; for by strength shall no man prevail.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />The adversaries of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall be broken to pieces; out of heaven shall he thunder upon them: the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall judge the ends of the earth; and he shall give strength unto his king, and exalt the horn of his anointed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Elkanah <char style="add">[God Has Taken Possession]</char> went to Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> to his house. And the child did minister unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> before ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char> the priest.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Now the sons of ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension] [were]</char> sons of Belial <char style="add">[Worthless, Good for Nothing]</char>; they knew not the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the priests’ custom with the people <char style="add">[was, that]</char>, when any man offered sacrifice, the priest’s servant came, while the flesh was in seething, with a fleshhook of three teeth in his hand;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he struck <char style="add">[it]</char> into the pan, or kettle, or caldron, or pot; all that the fleshhook brought up the priest took for himself. So they did in Shiloh <char style="add">[Place of Rest]</char> unto all the Yisra’eli’s that came there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Also before they burnt the fat, the priest’s servant came, and said to the man that sacrificed, Give flesh to roast for the priest; for he will not have coocked <char style="pn">(boiled)</char> flesh of you<char style="ord">i</char>, but raw.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And <char style="add">[if]</char> any man said unto him, Let them not fail to burn the fat presently, and <char style="add">[then]</char> take <char style="add">[as much]</char> as your<char style="ord">i</char> soul desires; then he would answer him, <char style="add">[No]</char>; but you<char style="ord">i</char> shall give <char style="add">[it me]</char> now: and if not, I will take <char style="add">[it]</char> by force.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />For what reason the sin of the young men was very great before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: for men abhorred the offering of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />But Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> ministered before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[being]</char> a child, girded with a linen ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Moreover his mother made him a little coat, and brought <char style="add">[it]</char> to him from year to year, when she came up with her husband to offer the yearly sacrifice.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char> Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> Elkanah <char style="add">[God Has Taken Possession]</char> and his wife, and said, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> give you<char style="ord">i</char> seed of this woman for the loan which is lent to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And they went unto their own home.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> visited Hannah <char style="add">[grace]</char>, so that she conceived, and bore three sons and two daughters. And the child Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> grew before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Now ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char> was very old, and heard all that his sons did unto all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and how they lay with the women that assembled <char style="add">[at]</char> the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And he said unto them, Why do you<char style="ord">2f</char> such things? for I hear of your evil dealings by all this people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />No, my sons; for <char style="add">[it is]</char> no good report that I hear: you<char style="ord">2f</char> make the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> people to transgress.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />If one man sin against another, the judge shall judge him: but if a man sin against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, who shall entreat for him? Yet they listened not unto the voice of their father, because the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> would slay them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And the child Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> grew on, and was in favour both with the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and also with men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And there came a man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> unto ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char>, and said unto him, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Did I plainly appear unto the house of you<char style="ord">i</char> father, when they were in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> in Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> house?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And did I choose him out of all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [to be]</char> my priest, to offer upon my altar, to burn incense, to wear an ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char> before me? and did I give unto the house of you<char style="ord">i</char> father all the offerings made by fire of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />For what reason kick you<char style="ord">2f</char> at my sacrifice and at my offering, which I have commanded <char style="add">[in my]</char> habitation; and honour you<char style="ord">i</char> sons above me, to make yourselves fat with the most important of all the offerings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> my people?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />For what reason the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> says, I said indeed <char style="add">[that]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> house, and the house of you<char style="ord">i</char> father, should walk before me forever: but now the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> says, Be it far from me; for them that honour me I will honour, and they that despise me shall be lightly esteemed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Behold, the days come, that I will cut off you<char style="ord">i</char> arm, and the arm of you<char style="ord">i</char> father’s house, that there shall not be an old man in you<char style="ord">i</char> house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall see an enemy <char style="add">[in my]</char> habitation, in all <char style="add">[the wealth]</char> which <char style="add">[God-Elōhīm (The Living Word) [The Many Powered]]</char> shall give Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and there shall not be an old man in you<char style="ord">i</char> house forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And the man of you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[whom]</char> I shall not cut off from my altar, <char style="add">[shall be]</char> to consume you<char style="ord">i</char> eyes, and to grieve you<char style="ord">i</char> heart: and all the increase of you<char style="ord">i</char> house shall die in the flower of their age.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And this <char style="add">[shall be]</char> a sign unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, that shall come upon your<char style="ord">i</char> two sons, on Hofni <char style="add">[fighter]</char> and Pinchas <char style="add">[mouth of brass]</char>; in one day they shall die both of them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And I will raise me up a faithful priest, <char style="add">[that]</char> shall do according to <char style="add">[that]</char> which <char style="add">[is]</char> in my heart and in my mind: and I will build him a sure house; and he shall walk before my anointed forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> everyone that is left in you<char style="ord">i</char> house shall come <char style="add">[and]</char> crouch to him for a piece of silver and a morsel of bread, and shall say, Put me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, into one of the priests’ offices, that I may eat a piece of bread.</para>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the child Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> ministered unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> before ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char>. And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was precious in those days; <char style="add">[there was]</char> no open vision.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And it came to pass at that time, when ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension] [was]</char> laid down in his place, and his eyes began to grow <char style="pn">(become; advance)</char> dim, <char style="add">[that]</char> he could not see;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And before the lamp of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> went out in the temple of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, where the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [was]</char>, and Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> was laid down <char style="add">[to sleep]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />That the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> called Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>: and he answered, Here <char style="add">[am]</char> I.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he ran unto ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char>, and said, Here <char style="add">[am]</char> I; for you<char style="ord">i</char> called me. And he said, I called not; lie down again. And he went and lay down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> called yet again, Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>. And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> arose and went to ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char>, and said, Here <char style="add">[am]</char> I; for you<char style="ord">i</char> did call me. And he answered, I called not, my son; lie down again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Now Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> did not yet know the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, neither was the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> yet revealed unto him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> called Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> again the third time. And he arose and went to ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char>, and said, Here <char style="add">[am]</char> I; for you<char style="ord">i</char> did call me. And ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char> perceived that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had called the child.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Therefore ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char> said unto Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, Go, lie down: and it shall be, if he call you<char style="ord">i</char>, that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall say, Speak, LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; for you<char style="ord">i</char> servant hears. So Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> went and lay down in his place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came, and stood, and called as at other times, Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>. Then Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> answered, Speak; for you<char style="ord">i</char> servant hears.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said to Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, Behold, I will do a thing in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, at which both the ears of everyone that hears it shall tingle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />In that day I will perform against ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char> all <char style="add">[things]</char> which I have spoken concerning his house: when I begin, I will also make an end.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />For I have told him that I will judge his house forever for the iniquity which he knows; because his sons made themselves vile, and he restrained them not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And therefore I have sworn unto the house of ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char>, that the iniquity of ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char>’s house shall not be purged with sacrifice nor offering forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> lay until the morning, and opened the doors of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> feared to show ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char> the vision.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Then ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char> called Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, and said, Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, my son. And he answered, Here <char style="add">[am]</char> I.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And he said, What <char style="add">[is]</char> the thing that [the LORD-Yehōvah (Messiah Pre-Incarnate)] has said unto you<char style="ord">i</char>? I pray you<char style="ord">i</char> hide <char style="add">[it]</char> not from me: God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> do so to you<char style="ord">i</char>, and more also, if you<char style="ord">i</char> hide <char style="add">[any]</char> thing from me of all the things that he said unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> told him every whit, and hid nothing from him. And he said, It <char style="add">[is]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: let him do what seems him good.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> grew, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was with him, and did let none of his words fall to <char style="pn">(to do entirely, do wholly)</char> the ground.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> from Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char> even to Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char> knew that Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El] [was]</char> established <char style="add">[to be]</char> a prophet of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> appeared again in Shiloh <char style="add">[Place of Rest]</char>: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> revealed himself to Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> in Shiloh <char style="add">[Place of Rest]</char> by the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the word of Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> came to all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>. Now Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went out against the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> to battle, and pitched beside Even-’’Ezer <char style="add">[treasure] [stone of help]</char>: and the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> pitched in Aphek <char style="add">[Enclosure]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> put themselves in array <char style="pn">(to put on; to clothe)</char> against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and when they joined battle, Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> was smitten before the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>: and they killed of the army in the field about four thousand men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And when the people were come into the camp, the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said, For what reason has the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> smitten us to day before the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>? Let us fetch the ark of the covenant of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> out of Shiloh <char style="add">[Place of Rest]</char> unto us, that, when it comes among us, it may save us out of the hand of our enemies.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />So the people sent to Shiloh <char style="add">[Place of Rest]</char>, that they might bring from there the ark of the covenant of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, which dwells <char style="add">[between]</char> the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char>: and the two sons of ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char>, Hofni <char style="add">[fighter]</char> and Pinchas <char style="add">[mouth of brass]</char>, <char style="add">[were]</char> there with the ark of the covenant of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And when the ark of the covenant of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came into the camp, all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shouted with a great shout, so that the earth rang again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And when the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> heard the noise of the shout, they said, What <char style="add">[means]</char> the noise of this great shout in the camp of the ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char>? And they understood that the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was come into the camp.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> were afraid, for they said, God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> is come into the camp. And they said, Woe unto us! for there has not been such a thing heretofore.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Woe unto us! who shall deliver us out of the hand of these mighty Gods? these <char style="add">[are]</char> the Gods that struck the Mitzri with all the plagues in the wilderness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Be strong, and quit <char style="pn">(acquitted; found not guilty)</char> yourselves like men, O you<char style="ord">2f</char> P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> be not servants unto the ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char>, as they have been to you: quit <char style="pn">(acquitted; found not guilty)</char> yourselves like men, and fight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> fought, and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> was smitten, and they fled every man into his tent: and there was a very great slaughter; for there fell of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> thirty thousand footmen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> was taken; and the two sons of ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char>, Hofni <char style="add">[fighter]</char> and Pinchas <char style="add">[mouth of brass]</char>, were slain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And there ran a man of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> out of the army, and came to Shiloh <char style="add">[Place of Rest]</char> the same day with his clothes rent, and with earth upon his head.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And when he came, lo, ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char> sat upon a seat by the wayside watching: for his heart trembled for the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>. And when the man came into the city, and told <char style="add">[it]</char>, all the city cried out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And when ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char> heard the noise of the crying, he said, What <char style="add">[means]</char> the noise of this tumult? And the man came in hastily, and told ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Now ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char> was ninety and eight years old; and his eyes were dim, that he could not see.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the man said unto ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char>, I <char style="add">[am]</char> he that came out of the army, and I fled to day out of the army. And he said, What is there done, my son?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the messenger answered and said, Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> is fled before the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and there has been also a great slaughter among the people, and you<char style="ord">i</char> two sons also, Hofni <char style="add">[fighter]</char> and Pinchas <char style="add">[mouth of brass]</char>, are dead, and the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> is taken.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And it came to pass, when he made mention of the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, that he fell from off the seat backward by the side of the gate, and his neck broke, and he died: for he was an old man, and heavy. And he had judged Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> forty years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And his daughter in law, Pinchas <char style="add">[mouth of brass]</char>’ wife, was with child, <char style="add">[near]</char> to be delivered: and when she heard the tidings that the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> was taken, and that her father in law and her husband were dead, she bowed herself and travailed; for her pains came upon her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And about the time of her death the women that stood by her said unto her, Fear not; for you<char style="ord">i</char> have born a son. But she answered not, neither did she regard <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And she named the child I-Khavod, saying, The glory is departed from Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: because the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> was taken, and because of her father in law and her husband.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And she said, The glory is departed from Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: for the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> is taken.</para>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> took the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and brought it from Even-’’Ezer <char style="add">[treasure] [stone of help]</char> unto Ashdod <char style="add">[powerful]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />When the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> took the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, they brought it into the house of Dagon, and set it by Dagon.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And when they of Ashdod <char style="add">[powerful]</char> arose early on the morrow, behold, Dagon <char style="add">[was]</char> fallen upon his face to the earth before the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And they took Dagon, and set him in his place again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And when they arose early on the morrow morning, behold, Dagon <char style="add">[was]</char> fallen upon his face to the ground before the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and the head of Dagon and both the palms of his hands <char style="add">[were]</char> cut off upon the threshold; only <char style="add">[the stump of]</char> Dagon was left to him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Therefore neither the priests of Dagon, nor any that come into Dagon’s house, trample on the threshold of Dagon in Ashdod <char style="add">[powerful]</char> unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />But the hand of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was heavy upon them of Ashdod <char style="add">[powerful]</char>, and he destroyed them, and struck them with hemorrhoids, <char style="add">[even]</char> Ashdod <char style="add">[powerful]</char> and the coasts thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And when the men of Ashdod <char style="add">[powerful]</char> saw that <char style="add">[it was]</char> so, they said, The ark of the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall not abide with us: for his hand is sore upon us, and upon Dagon our god.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />They sent therefore and gathered all the lords of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> unto them, and said, What shall we do with the ark of the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>? And they answered, Let the ark of the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> be carried about unto Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>. And they carried the ark of the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> about <char style="add">[there]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And it was <char style="add">[so]</char>, that, after they had carried it about, the hand of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was against the city with a very great destruction: and he struck the men of the city, both small and great, and they had hemorrhoids in their secret parts.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Therefore they sent the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> to ‘Ekron <char style="add">[Torn Up by the Roots]</char>. And it came to pass, as the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> came to ‘Ekron <char style="add">[Torn Up by the Roots]</char>, that the ‘Ekron <char style="add">[Torn Up by the Roots]</char> cried out, saying, They have brought about the ark of the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to us, to slay us and our people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />So they sent and gathered together all the lords of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and said, Send away the ark of the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and let it go again to his own place, that it slay us not, and our people: for there was a deadly destruction throughout all the city; the hand of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> was very heavy there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the men that died not were smitten with the hemorrhoids: and the cry of the city went up to heaven.</para>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was in the country of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> seven months.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> called for the priests and the diviners, saying, What shall we do to the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>? tell us which we shall send it to his place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And they said, If you<char style="ord">2f</char> send away the ark of the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, send it not empty; but in any wise return him a trespass offering: then you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall be healed, and it shall be known to you why his hand is not removed from you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then said they, What <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the trespass offering which we shall return to him? They answered, Five golden hemorrhoids, and five golden mice, <char style="add">[according to]</char> the number of the lords of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>: for one plague <char style="add">[was]</char> on you all, and on your lords.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />For what reason you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall make images of your hemorrhoids, and images of your mice that mar the land; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall give glory unto the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: perhaps he will lighten his hand from off you, and from off your gods, and from off your land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />For what reason then do you<char style="ord">2f</char> harden your hearts, as the Mitzri and Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> hardened their hearts? when he had wrought wonderfully among them, did they not let the people go, and they departed?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Now therefore make a new cart, and take two milk cattle, on which there has come no yoke, and tie the cattle to the cart, and bring their calves home from them:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And take the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and lay it upon the cart; and put the jewels of gold, which you<char style="ord">2f</char> return him <char style="add">[for]</char> a trespass offering, in a coffer by the side thereof; and send it away, that it may go.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And see, if it goes up by the way of his own coast to Beit-Shemesh <char style="add">[House of the Sun]</char>, <char style="add">[then]</char> he has done us this great evil: but if not, then we shall know that <char style="add">[it is]</char> not his hand <char style="add">[that]</char> struck us: it <char style="add">[was]</char> a chance <char style="add">[that]</char> happened to us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the men did so; and took two milk cattle, and tied them to the cart, and shut up their calves at home:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And they laid the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> upon the cart, and the coffer with the mice of gold and the images of their hemorrhoids.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the cattle took the straight way to the way of Beit-Shemesh <char style="add">[House of the Sun]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> went along the highway, lowing as they went, and turned not aside <char style="add">[to]</char> the right hand or <char style="add">[to]</char> the left; and the lords of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> went after them unto the border of Beit-Shemesh <char style="add">[House of the Sun]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And <char style="add">[they of]</char> Beit-Shemesh <char style="add">[House of the Sun] [were]</char> reaping their wheat harvest in the valley: and they lifted up their eyes, and saw the ark, and rejoiced to see <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the cart came into the field of Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char>, a Beit-Shimshi <char style="add">[house of the sun]</char>, and stood there, where <char style="add">[there was]</char> a great stone: and they clave the wood of the cart, and offered the cattle a burnt offering unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> took down the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the coffer that <char style="add">[was]</char> with it, wherein the jewels of gold <char style="add">[were]</char>, and put <char style="add">[them]</char> on the great stone: and the men of Beit-Shemesh <char style="add">[House of the Sun]</char> offered burnt offerings and sacrificed sacrifices the same day unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And when the five lords of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> had seen <char style="add">[it]</char>, they returned to ‘Ekron <char style="add">[Torn Up by the Roots]</char> the same day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And these <char style="add">[are]</char> the golden hemorrhoids which the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> returned <char style="add">[for]</char> a trespass offering unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; for Ashdod <char style="add">[powerful]</char> one, for ‘Azah <char style="add">[The Strong]</char> one, for Askelon [The Fire of Infamy: I shall be Weighed] one, for Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char> one, for ‘Ekron <char style="add">[Torn Up by the Roots]</char> one;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the golden mice, <char style="add">[according to]</char> the number of all the cities of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants] [belonging]</char> to the five lords, <char style="add">[both]</char> of fenced cities, and of country villages, even unto the great <char style="add">[stone of]</char> Hevel <char style="pn">(herdsman)</char>, whereon they set down the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: <char style="add">[which stone remains]</char> unto this day in the field of Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char>, the Beit-Shimshi <char style="add">[house of the sun]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And he struck the men of Beit-Shemesh <char style="add">[House of the Sun]</char>, because they had looked into the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, even he struck of the people fifty thousand and threescore and ten men: and the people lamented, because the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had smitten <char style="add">[many]</char> of the people with a great slaughter.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the men of Beit-Shemesh <char style="add">[House of the Sun]</char> said, Who is able to stand before this holy LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>? and to whom shall he go up from us?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And they sent messengers to the inhabitants of Kiryat-Ye’arim <char style="add">[City of Forests]</char>, saying, The P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> have brought again the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; come you<char style="ord">2f</char> down, <char style="add">[and]</char> fetch it up to you.</para>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the men of Kiryat-Ye’arim <char style="add">[City of Forests]</char> came, and fetched up the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and brought it into the house of Avinadav <char style="add">[my father is noble]</char> in the hill, and sanctified El’azar <char style="add">[God has helped]</char> his son to keep the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And it came to pass, while the ark abode in Kiryat-Ye’arim <char style="add">[City of Forests]</char>, that the time was long; for it was twenty years: and all the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> lamented after the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> spoke unto all the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, If you<char style="ord">2f</char> do return unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> with all your hearts, <char style="add">[then]</char> put away the strange gods and ‘Ashtarot <char style="add">[Star (female deity)]</char> from among you, and prepare your hearts unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and serve him only: and he will deliver you out of the hand of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> did put away Ba’alim <char style="add">[lords (false gods)]</char> and ‘Ashtarot <char style="add">[Star (female deity)]</char>, and served the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> only.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said, Gather all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char>, and I will pray for you unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And they gathered together to Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char>, and drew water, and poured <char style="add">[it]</char> out before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and fasted on that day, and said there, We have sinned against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> judged the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And when the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> heard that the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> were gathered together to Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char>, the lords of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> went up against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>. And when the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> heard <char style="add">[it]</char>, they were afraid of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said to Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, Cease not to cry unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> for us, that he will save us out of the hand of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> took a sucking lamb, and offered <char style="add">[it for]</char> a burnt offering wholly unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> cried unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> for Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> heard him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And as Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> was offering up the burnt offering, the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> drew near to battle against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: but the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> thundered with a great thunder on that day upon the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and scattered <char style="pn">(defeated in battle)</char> them; and they were smitten before Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went out of Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char>, and pursued the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and struck them, until <char style="add">[they came]</char> under Beit-Kar <char style="add">[house of the ram]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Then Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> took a stone, and set <char style="add">[it]</char> between Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char> and Shen <char style="add">[crag]</char>, and called the name of it Even-’’Ezer <char style="add">[treasure] [stone of help]</char>, saying, Until now has the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> helped us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />So the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> were subdued, and they came no more into the coast of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and the hand of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was against the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> all the days of Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the cities which the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> had taken from Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> were restored to Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, from ‘Ekron <char style="add">[Torn Up by the Roots]</char> even unto Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>; and the coasts thereof did Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> deliver out of the hands of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>. And there was peace between Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> judged Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> all the days of his life.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he went from year to year in circuit to Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>, and Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>, and Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char>, and judged Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in all those places.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And his return <char style="add">[was]</char> to Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>; for there <char style="add">[was]</char> his house; and there he judged Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and there he built an altar unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> was old, that he made his sons over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Now the name of his firstborn was Yo’el <char style="add">[Yehovah is God]</char>; and the name of his second, Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char>: <char style="add">[they were]</char> in Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And his sons walked not in his ways, but turned aside after profit, and took bribes, and perverted judgment.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then all the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> gathered themselves together, and came to Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> unto Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And said unto him, Behold, you<char style="ord">i</char> are old, and your<char style="ord">i</char> sons walk not in your<char style="ord">i</char> ways: now make us a king to judge us like all the nations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />But the thing displeased Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, when they said, Give us a king to judge us. And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> prayed unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, Listen unto the voice of the people in all that they say unto you<char style="ord">i</char>: for they have not rejected you<char style="ord">i</char>, but they have rejected me, that I should not reign over them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />According to all the works which they have done since the day that I brought them up out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> even unto this day, which they have forsaken me, and served other gods, so do they also unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Now therefore hearken unto their voice: howbeit yet protest solemnly unto them, and show them the manner of the king that shall reign over them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> told all the words of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> unto the people that asked of him a king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And he said, This will be the manner of the king that shall reign over you: He will take your sons, and appoint <char style="add">[them]</char> for himself, for his chariots, and <char style="add">[to be]</char> his horsemen; and <char style="add">[some]</char> shall run before his chariots.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And he will appoint him captains over thousands, and captains over fifties; and <char style="add">[will set them]</char> to ear his ground, and to reap his harvest, and to make his instruments of war, and instruments of his chariots.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he will take your daughters <char style="add">[to be]</char> confectionaries <char style="pn">(perfume/oiintment makeers; perfumers)</char>, and <char style="add">[to be]</char> cooks, and <char style="add">[to be]</char> bakers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he will take your fields, and your vineyards, and your olive yards, <char style="add">[even]</char> the best <char style="add">[of them]</char>, and give <char style="add">[them]</char> to his servants.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he will take the tenth of your seed, and of your vineyards, and give to his officers, and to his servants.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he will take your menservants, and your maidservants, and your goodliest young men, and your asses, and put <char style="add">[them]</char> to his work.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />He will take the tenth of your sheep: and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall be his servants.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall cry out in that day because of your king which you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall have chosen you; and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will not hear you in that day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Nevertheless the people refused to obey the voice of Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>; and they said, No; but we will have a king over us;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />That we also may be like all the nations; and that our king may judge us, and go out before us, and fight our battles.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> heard all the words of the people, and he rehearsed them in the ears of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said to Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, Listen unto their voice, and make them a king. And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said unto the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Go you<char style="ord">2f</char> every man unto his city.</para>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now there was a man of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, whose name <char style="add">[was]</char> Kish <char style="add">[bent]</char>, the son of Avi’el <char style="add">[El (God) is my father]</char>, the son of Tz’ror <char style="add">[parcel]</char>, the son of B’khorat <char style="add">[first-born]</char>, the son of Afiach <char style="add">[I will make to breathe]</char>, from the tribe of Binyamin <char style="add">[A Son of the Right Hand]</char>, a mighty man of power.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he had a son, whose name <char style="add">[was]</char> Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, a choice young man, and a goodly: and <char style="add">[there was]</char> not among the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> a goodlier person than he: from his shoulders and upward <char style="add">[he was]</char> higher than any of the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the asses of Kish <char style="add">[bent]</char> Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> father were lost. And Kish <char style="add">[bent]</char> said to Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> his son, Take now one of the servants with you<char style="ord">i</char>, and arise, go seek the asses.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he passed through mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, and passed through the land of Shalishah <char style="add">[night monster; hobgoblin]</char>, but they found <char style="add">[them]</char> not: then they passed through the land of Sha’alim <char style="add">[foxes]</char>, and <char style="add">[there they were]</char> not: and he passed through the land of the Binyamini, but they found <char style="add">[them]</char> not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[And]</char> when they were come to the land of Tzuf <char style="add">[honeycomb]</char>, Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said to his servant that <char style="add">[was]</char> with him, Come, and let us return; lest my father leave <char style="add">[caring]</char> for the asses, and take thought for us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he said unto him, Behold now, <char style="add">[there is]</char> in this city a man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and <char style="add">[he is]</char> an honourable man; all that he says comes surely to pass: now let us go there; perhaps he can show us our way that we should go.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Then said Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> to his servant, But, behold, <char style="add">[if]</char> we go, what shall we bring the man? for the bread is spent in our vessels, and <char style="add">[there is]</char> not a present to bring to the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: what have we?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the servant answered Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> again, and said, Behold, I have here at hand the fourth part of a shekel of silver: <char style="add">[that]</char> will I give to the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, to tell us our way.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />(Beforetime in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, when a man went to enquire of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, thus he spoke, Come, and let us go to the seer: for <char style="add">[he that is]</char> now <char style="add">[called]</char> a Prophet was formerly called a Seer.)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Then said Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> to his servant, Well said; come, let us go. So they went unto the city where the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [was]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[And]</char> as they went up the hill to the city, they found young maidens going out to draw water, and said unto them, Is the seer here?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And they answered them, and said, He is; behold, <char style="add">[he is]</char> before you: make haste now, for he came to day to the city; for <char style="add">[there is]</char> a sacrifice of the people to day in the high place:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />As soon as you<char style="ord">2f</char> be come into the city, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall immediately find him, before he go up to the high place to eat: for the people will not eat until he come, because he does bless the sacrifice; <char style="add">[and]</char> afterwards they eat that be bidden. Now therefore get you up; for about this time you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall find him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And they went up into the city: <char style="add">[and]</char> when they were come into the city, behold, Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> came out against them, for to go up to the high place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Now the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had told Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> in his ear a day before Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> came, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Tomorrow about this time I will send you<char style="ord">i</char> a man out of the land of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall anoint him <char style="add">[to be]</char> captain over my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that he may save my people out of the hand of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>: for I have looked upon my people, because their cry is come unto me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And when Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> saw Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto him, Behold the man whom I spoke to you<char style="ord">i</char> of! this same shall reign over my people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> drew near to Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> in the gate, and said, Tell me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, where the seer’s house <char style="add">[is]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> answered Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and said, I <char style="add">[am]</char> the seer: go up before me unto the high place; for you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall eat with me to day, and tomorrow I will let you<char style="ord">i</char> go, and will tell you<char style="ord">i</char> all that <char style="add">[is]</char> in you<char style="ord">i</char> heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And as for you<char style="ord">i</char> asses that were lost three days ago, set not you<char style="ord">i</char> mind on them; for they are found. And on whom <char style="add">[is]</char> all the desire of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>? <char style="add">[Is it]</char> not on you<char style="ord">i</char>, and on all you<char style="ord">i</char> father’s house?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> answered and said, <char style="add">[Am]</char> not I from the tribe of Binyamin <char style="add">[A Son of the Right Hand]</char>, of the smallest of the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>? and my family the least of all the families of the tribe of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>? wherefore then speak you<char style="ord">i</char> so to me?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> took Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and his servant, and brought them into the parlour, and made them sit in the most important place among them that were bidden, which <char style="add">[were]</char> about thirty persons.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said unto the cook, Bring the portion which I gave you<char style="ord">i</char>, of which I said unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, Set it by you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the cook took up the shoulder, and <char style="add">[that]</char> which <char style="add">[was]</char> upon it, and set <char style="add">[it]</char> before Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>. And [Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>] said, Behold that which is left! set <char style="add">[it]</char> before you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> eat: for unto this time has it been kept for you<char style="ord">i</char> since I said, I have invited the people. So Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> did eat with Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> that day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And when they were come down from the high place into the city, [Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>] communed with Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> upon the top of the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And they arose early: and it came to pass about the spring of the day, that Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> called Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> to the top of the house, saying, Up, that I may send you<char style="ord">i</char> away. And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> arose, and they went out both of them, he and Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, abroad.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[And]</char> as they were going down to the end of the city, Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said to Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, Bid the servant pass on before us, <char style="pn">(and he passed on,)</char> but stand you<char style="ord">i</char> still a while, that I may show you<char style="ord">i</char> the word of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> took a vial of oil, and poured <char style="add">[it]</char> upon his head, and kissed him, and said, <char style="add">[Is it]</char> not because the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has anointed you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[to be]</char> captain over his inheritance?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />When you<char style="ord">i</char> are departed from me today, then you<char style="ord">i</char> shall find two men by Rachel’s <char style="add">[ewe]</char> sepulcher in the border of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> at Tzeltzah <char style="add">[shadow]</char>; and they will say unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, The asses which you<char style="ord">i</char> went to seek are found: and, lo, you<char style="ord">i</char> father has left the care of the asses, and sorrows for you, saying, What shall I do for my son?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Then shall you<char style="ord">i</char> go on forward from here, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall come to the plain of Tavor <char style="add">[Mound]</char>, and there shall meet you<char style="ord">i</char> three men going up to God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> to Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>, one carrying three kids, and another carrying three loaves of bread, and another carrying a bottle of wine:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And they will salute you<char style="ord">i</char>, and give you<char style="ord">i</char> two <char style="add">[loaves]</char> of bread; which you<char style="ord">i</char> shall receive of their hands.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />After that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall come to the hill of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, where <char style="add">[is]</char> the Garrison <char style="pn">(fortification; military post)</char> of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>: and it shall come to pass, when you<char style="ord">i</char> are come there to the city, that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall meet a company of prophets coming down from the high place with a Psaltery <char style="pn">(stringed instrument, like an harp)</char>, and a tambourine, and a pipe, and a harp, before them; and they shall prophesy:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the Spirit of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will come upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall prophesy with them, and shall be turned into another man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And let it be, when these signs are come unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[that]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> do as occasion serve you<char style="ord">i</char>; for God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [is]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall go down before me to Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>; and, behold, I will come down unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, to offer burnt offerings, <char style="add">[and]</char> to sacrifice sacrifices of peace offerings: seven days shall you<char style="ord">i</char> wait, till I come to you<char style="ord">i</char>, and show you<char style="ord">i</char> what you<char style="ord">i</char> shall do.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And it was <char style="add">[so]</char>, that when he had turned his back to go from Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> gave him another heart: and all those signs came to pass that day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And when they came there to the hill, behold, a company of prophets met him; and the Spirit of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> came upon him, and he prophesied among them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And it came to pass, when all that knew him formerly saw that, behold, he prophesied among the prophets, then the people said one to another, What <char style="add">[is]</char> this <char style="add">[that]</char> is come unto the son of Kish <char style="add">[bent]</char>? <char style="add">[Is]</char> Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> also among the prophets?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And one of the same place answered and said, But who <char style="add">[is]</char> their father? Therefore it became a proverb, <char style="add">[Is]</char> Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> also among the prophets?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And when he had made an end of prophesying, he came to the high place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> uncle said unto him and to his servant, Where went you<char style="ord">2f</char>? And he said, To seek the asses: and when we saw that <char style="add">[they were]</char> nowhere, we came to Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> uncle said, Tell me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, what Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said unto you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said unto his uncle, He told us plainly that the asses were found. But of the matter of the kingdom, whereof Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> spoke, he told him not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> called the people together unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> to Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And said unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, I brought up Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and delivered you out of the hand of the Mitzri, and out of the hand of all kingdoms, <char style="add">[and]</char> of them that oppressed you:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> have this day rejected your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, who himself saved you out of all your adversities and your tribulations; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> have said unto him, <char style="add">[No]</char>, but set a king over us. Now therefore present yourselves before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> by your tribes, and by your thousands.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And when Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> had caused all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to come near, the tribe of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> was taken.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />When he had caused the tribe of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> to come near by their families, the family of Matri <char style="add">[rain of Yehovah]</char> was taken, and Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> the son of Kish <char style="add">[bent]</char> was taken: and when they sought him, he could not be found.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Therefore they enquired of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> further, if the man should yet come there. And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> answered, Behold, he has hid himself among the stuff.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And they ran and fetched him there: and when he stood among the people, he was higher than any of the people from his shoulders and upward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said to all the people, See you<char style="ord">2f</char> him whom the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has chosen, that <char style="add">[there is]</char> none like him among all the people? And all the people shouted, and said, Long live the king!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Then Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> told the people the manner of the kingdom, and wrote <char style="add">[it]</char> in a book, and laid <char style="add">[it]</char> up before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> sent all the people away, every man to his house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> also went home to Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>; and there went with him a band of men, whose hearts God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> had touched.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />But the children of Belial <char style="add">[Worthless, Good for Nothing]</char> said, How shall this man save us? And they despised him, and brought him no presents. But he held his peace.</para>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then Nachash <char style="add">[serpent]</char> the ‘Amoni <char style="add">[tribal]</char> came up, and encamped against Yavesh-Gil’ad <char style="add">[Dry Hill of Testimony]</char>: and all the men of Yavesh <char style="add">[dry]</char> said unto Nachash <char style="add">[serpent]</char>, Make a covenant with us, and we will serve you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Nachash <char style="add">[serpent]</char> the ‘Amoni <char style="add">[tribal]</char> answered them, On this <char style="add">[condition]</char> will I make <char style="add">[a covenant]</char> with you, that I may thrust out all your right eyes, and lay it <char style="add">[for]</char> a reproach <char style="pn">(disgrace; shame)</char> upon all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the elders of Yavesh <char style="add">[dry]</char> said unto him, Give us seven days’ respite, that we may send messengers unto all the coasts of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and then, if <char style="add">[there be]</char> no man to save us, we will come out to you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then came the messengers to Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and told the tidings in the ears of the people: and all the people lifted up their voices, and wept.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And, behold, Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> came after the herd out of the field; and Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said, What <char style="add">[ails]</char> the people that they weep? And they told him the tidings of the men of Yavesh <char style="add">[dry]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the Spirit of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> came upon Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> when he heard those tidings, and his anger was kindled greatly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he took a yoke of oxen, and hewed them in pieces, and sent <char style="add">[them]</char> throughout all the coasts of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> by the hands of messengers, saying, Whosoever comes not forth after Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and after Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, so shall it be done unto his oxen. And the fear of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> fell on the people, and they came out with one consent.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And when he numbered them in Bezek <char style="add">[Lightning]</char>, the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> were three hundred thousand, and the men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> thirty thousand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And they said unto the messengers that came, Thus shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> say unto the men of Yavesh-Gil’ad <char style="add">[Dry Hill of Testimony]</char>, Tomorrow, by <char style="add">[that time]</char> the sun be hot, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall have help. And the messengers came and showed <char style="add">[it]</char> to the men of Yavesh <char style="add">[dry]</char>; and they were glad.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Therefore the men of Yavesh <char style="add">[dry]</char> said, Tomorrow we will come out unto you, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall do with us all that seems good unto you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And it was <char style="add">[so]</char> on the morrow, that Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> put the people in three companies; and they came into the midst of the host in the morning watch, and killed the ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> until the heat of the day: and it came to pass, that they which remained were scattered, so that two of them were not left together.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the people said unto Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, Who <char style="add">[is]</char> he that said, Shall Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> reign over us? bring the men, that we may put them to death.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said, There shall not a man be put to death this day: for today the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has wrought salvation in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then said Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> to the people, Come, and let us go to Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>, and renew the kingdom there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And all the people went to Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>; and there they made Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> king before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>; and there they sacrificed sacrifices of peace offerings before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and there Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and all the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> rejoiced greatly.</para>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said unto all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Behold, I have listened unto your voice in all that you<char style="ord">2f</char> said unto me, and have made a king over you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And now, behold, the king walks before you: and I am old and grayheaded; and, behold, my sons <char style="add">[are]</char> with you: and I have walked before you from my childhood unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Behold, here I <char style="add">[am]</char>: witness against me before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and before his anointed: whose ox have I taken? or whose ass have I taken? or whom have I defrauded? whom have I oppressed? or of whose hand have I received <char style="add">[any]</char> bribe to blind my eyes with that? and I will restore it you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And they said, you<char style="ord">i</char> have not defrauded us, nor oppressed us, neither have you<char style="ord">i</char> taken ought of any man’s hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he said unto them, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> witness against you, and his anointed <char style="add">[is]</char> witness this day, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> have not found ought in my hand. And they answered, <char style="add">[He is]</char> witness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said unto the people, <char style="add">[It is]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> that advanced Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, and that brought your fathers up out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Now therefore stand still, that I may reason with you before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> of all the righteous acts of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which he did to you and to your fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />When Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char> was come into Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and your fathers cried unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, then the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sent Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, which brought forth your fathers out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and made them dwell in this place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And when they forgot the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, he sold them into the hand of Sisra <char style="add">[Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)]</char>, captain of the host of Hatzor <char style="add">[Castle]</char>, and into the hand of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and into the hand of the king of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, and they fought against them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And they cried unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and said, We have sinned, because we have forsaken the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and have served Ba’alim [lords (false gods)] and ‘Ashtarot <char style="add">[Star (female deity)]</char>: but now deliver us out of the hand of our enemies, and we will serve you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sent Yeruba’al <char style="add">[let Ba’al defend]</char>, and B’dan <char style="add">[in judging]</char>, and Yiftach <char style="add">[He Opens]</char>, and Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, and delivered you out of the hand of your enemies on every side, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> dwelled safe.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And when you<char style="ord">2f</char> saw that Nachash <char style="add">[serpent]</char> the king of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> came against you, you<char style="ord">2f</char> said unto me, No; but a king shall reign over us: when the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [was]</char> your king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Now therefore behold the king whom you<char style="ord">2f</char> have chosen, <char style="add">[and]</char> whom you<char style="ord">2f</char> have desired! and, behold, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has set a king over you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />If you<char style="ord">2f</char> will fear the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and serve him, and obey his voice, and not rebel against the commandment of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, then shall both you<char style="ord">2f</char> and also the king that reigns over you continue following the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />But if you<char style="ord">2f</char> will not obey the voice of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, but rebel against the commandment of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, then shall the hand of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> be against you, as <char style="add">[it was]</char> against your fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Now therefore stand and see this great thing, which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will do before your eyes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Is it]</char> not wheat harvest to day? I will call unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and he shall send thunder and rain; that you<char style="ord">2f</char> may perceive and see that your wickedness <char style="add">[is]</char> great, which you<char style="ord">2f</char> have done in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, in asking you a king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />So Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> called unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sent thunder and rain that day: and all the people greatly feared the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> and Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And all the people said unto Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, Pray for you<char style="ord">i</char> servants unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, that we die not: for we have added unto all our sins <char style="add">[this]</char> evil, to ask us a king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said unto the people, Fear not: you<char style="ord">2f</char> have done all this wickedness: yet turn not aside from following the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, but serve the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> with all your heart;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And turn you<char style="ord">2f</char> not aside: for [then should you<char style="ord">2f</char> go] after vain <char style="add">[things]</char>, which cannot profit nor deliver; for they <char style="add">[are]</char> vain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />For the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will not forsake his people for his great name’s sake: because it has pleased the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> to make you his people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Moreover as for me, God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> forbid that I should sin against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in ceasing to pray for you: but I will teach you the good and the right way:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Only fear the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and serve him in twith all your heart: for consider how great <char style="add">[things]</char> he has done for you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />But if you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall still do wickedly, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall be consumed, both you<char style="ord">2f</char> and your king.</para>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> reigned one year; and when he had reigned two years over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> chose him three thousand <char style="add">[men]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; <char style="add">[whereof]</char> two thousand were with Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> in Mikhmas <char style="add">[hidden]</char> and in mount Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>, and a thousand were with Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> in Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>: and the rest of the people he sent every man to his tent.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> struck the Garrison <char style="pn">(fortification; military post)</char> of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> that <char style="add">[was]</char> in Geva <char style="add">[hill]</char>, and the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> heard <char style="add">[of it]</char>. And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> blew the trumpet throughout all the land, saying, Let the ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char> hear.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> heard say <char style="add">[that]</char> Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> had smitten a Garrison <char style="pn">(fortification; military post)</char> of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and <char style="add">[that]</char> Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> also was had in abomination with the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>. And the people were called together after Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> to Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> gathered themselves together to fight with Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, thirty thousand chariots, and six thousand horsemen, and people as the sand which <char style="add">[is]</char> on the sea shore in multitude: and they came up, and pitched in Mikhmas <char style="add">[hidden]</char>, eastward from Beit-On <char style="add">[vanity] [house of vanity]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />When the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> saw that they were in a strait, <char style="pn">(for the people were distressed,)</char> then the people did hide themselves in caves, and in thickets, and in rocks, and in high places, and in pits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And <char style="add">[some of]</char> the ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char> went over Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char> to the land of Gad <char style="add">[Good Fortune with Troublesome Effort]</char> and Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>. As for Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, he <char style="add">[was]</char> yet in Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>, and all the people followed him trembling.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And he tarried seven days, according to the set time that Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El] [had appointed]</char>: but Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> came not to Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>; and the people were scattered from him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said, Bring here a burnt offering to me, and peace offerings. And he offered the burnt offering.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And it came to pass, that as soon as he had made an end of offering the burnt offering, behold, Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> came; and Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> went out to meet him, that he might salute him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said, What have you<char style="ord">i</char> done? And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said, Because I saw that the people were scattered from me, and <char style="add">[that]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> came not within the days appointed, and <char style="add">[that]</char> the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> gathered themselves together at Mikhmas <char style="add">[hidden]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Therefore said I, The P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> will come down now upon me to Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>, and I have not made supplication unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: I forced myself therefore, and offered a burnt offering.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said to Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> have done foolishly: you<char style="ord">i</char> have not kept the commandment of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, which he commanded you<char style="ord">i</char>: for now would the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have established you<char style="ord">i</char> kingdom upon Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />But now you<char style="ord">i</char> kingdom shall not continue: the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has sought him a man after his own heart, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has commanded him <char style="add">[to be]</char> captain over his people, because you<char style="ord">i</char> have not kept <char style="add">[that]</char> which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> arose, and got him up from Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char> unto Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>. And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> numbered the people <char style="add">[that were]</char> present with him, about six hundred men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> his son, and the people <char style="add">[that were]</char> present with them, abode in Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>: but the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> encamped in Mikhmas <char style="add">[hidden]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the spoilers came out of the camp of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> in three companies: one company turned unto the way <char style="add">[that leads to]</char> ‘Ofrah <char style="add">[Fawn]</char>, unto the land of Shu’al <char style="add">[jackal]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And another company turned the way <char style="add">[to]</char> Beit-Horon <char style="add">[House of Hollowness]</char>: and another company turned <char style="add">[to]</char> the way of the border that looks to the valley of Tzvoyim <char style="add">[Gazelles]</char> toward the wilderness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Now there was no smith found throughout all the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: for the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> said, Lest the ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char> make <char style="add">[them]</char> swords or spears:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />But all the Yisra’eli’s went down to the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, to sharpen every man his share, and his coulter <char style="pn">(a sharp iron blade on the front of a plow that cuts into the soil)</char>, and his axe, and his mattock <char style="pn">(hoe or other tool to break up dirt)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Yet they had a file for the mattocks, and for the coulters, and for the forks, and for the axes, and to sharpen the goads.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />So it came to pass in the day of battle, that there was neither sword nor spear found in the hand of any of the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>: but with Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and with Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> his son was there found.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the Garrison <char style="pn">(fortification; military post)</char> of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> went out to the passage of Mikhmas <char style="add">[hidden]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="14" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now it came to pass upon a day, that Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> the son of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said unto the young man that bore his armour, Come, and let us go over to the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>’ Garrison <char style="pn">(fortification; military post)</char>, that <char style="add">[is]</char> on the other side. But he told not his father.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> tarried in the uttermost part of Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> under a pomegranate tree which <char style="add">[is]</char> in Migron <char style="add">[precipice]</char>: and the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him <char style="add">[were]</char> about six hundred men;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char>, the son of Achituv <char style="add">[my brother is good]</char>, I-Khavod’s brother, the son of Pinchas <char style="add">[mouth of brass]</char>, the son of ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char>, the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> priest in Shiloh <char style="add">[Place of Rest]</char>, wearing an ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>. And the people knew not that Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> was gone.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And between the passages, by which Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> sought to go over unto the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>’ Garrison <char style="pn">(fortification; military post)</char>, <char style="add">[there was]</char> a sharp rock on the one side, and a sharp rock on the other side: and the name of the one <char style="add">[was]</char> Botzetz <char style="add">[surpassing white; glistening]</char>, and the name of the other Seneh <char style="add">[thorny]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />The forefront of the one <char style="add">[was]</char> situate northward over against Mikhmas <char style="add">[hidden]</char>, and the other southward over against Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> said to the young man that bore his armour, Come, and let us go over unto the Garrison <char style="pn">(fortification; military post)</char> of these uncircumcised: it may be that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will work for us: for <char style="add">[there is]</char> no restraint to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> to save by many or by few.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And his armourbearer said unto him, Do all that <char style="add">[is]</char> in you<char style="ord">i</char> heart: turn you<char style="ord">i</char>; behold, I <char style="add">[am]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char> according to you<char style="ord">i</char> heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then said Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>, Behold, we will pass over unto <char style="add">[these]</char> men, and we will discover <char style="pn">(uncover; reveal; have first sight of)</char> ourselves unto them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />If they say thus unto us, Tarry until we come to you; then we will stand still in our place, and will not go up unto them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />But if they say thus, Come up unto us; then we will go up: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has delivered them into our hand: and this <char style="add">[shall be]</char> a sign unto us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And both of them discovered themselves unto the Garrison <char style="pn">(fortification; military post)</char> of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>: and the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> said, Behold, the ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char> come forth out of the holes where they had hid themselves.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the men of the Garrison <char style="pn">(fortification; military post)</char> answered Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> and his armourbearer, and said, Come up to us, and we will show you a thing. And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> said unto his armourbearer, Come up after me: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has delivered them into the hand of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> climbed up upon his hands and upon his feet, and his armourbearer after him: and they fell before Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>; and his armourbearer killed after him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And that first slaughter, which Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> and his armourbearer made, was about twenty men, within as it were an half acre of land, <char style="add">[which]</char> a yoke <char style="add">[of oxen might plow]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And there was trembling in the host, in the field, and among all the people: the Garrison <char style="pn">(fortification; military post)</char>, and the spoilers, they also trembled, and the earth quaked: so it was a very great trembling.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the watchmen of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> in Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> looked; and, behold, the multitude melted away, and they went on beating down <char style="add">[one another]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Then said Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> unto the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him, Number now, and see who is gone from us. And when they had numbered, behold, Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> and his armourbearer <char style="add">[were]</char> not <char style="add">[there]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said unto Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char>, Bring here the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>. For the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> was at that time with the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And it came to pass, while Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> talked unto the priest, that the noise that <char style="add">[was]</char> in the host of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> went on and increased: and Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said unto the priest, Withdraw you<char style="ord">i</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and all the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him assembled themselves, and they came to the battle: and, behold, every man’s sword was against his fellow, <char style="add">[and there was]</char> a very great discomfiture.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Moreover the ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew] [that]</char> were with the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> before that time, which went up with them into the camp <char style="add">[from the country]</char> round about, even they also <char style="add">[turned]</char> to be with the Yisra’eli’s that <char style="add">[were]</char> with Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Likewise all the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> which had hid themselves in mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, <char style="add">[when]</char> they heard that the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> fled, even they also followed hard after them in the battle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />So the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> saved Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that day: and the battle passed over unto Beit-On <char style="add">[vanity] [house of vanity]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> were distressed that day: for Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> had adjured the people, saying, Cursed <char style="add">[be]</char> the man that eats <char style="add">[any]</char> food until evening, that I may be avenged on my enemies. So none of the people tasted <char style="add">[any]</char> food.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And all <char style="add">[they of]</char> the land came to a wood; and there was honey upon the ground.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And when the people were come into the wood, behold, the honey dropped; but no man put his hand to his mouth: for the people feared the oath.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />But Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> heard not when his father charged the people with the oath: wherefore he put forth the end of the rod that <char style="add">[was]</char> in his hand, and dipped it in an honeycomb, and put his hand to his mouth; and his eyes were enlightened.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Then answered one of the people, and said, Your<char style="ord">1s</char> father straitly charged the people with an oath, saying, Cursed <char style="add">[be]</char> the man that eats <char style="add">[any]</char> food this day. And the people were faint.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Then said Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>, My father has troubled the land: see, I pray you, how my eyes have been enlightened, because I tasted a little of this honey.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />How much more, if perhaps <char style="pn">(maybe)</char> the people had eaten freely to day of the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> of their enemies which they found? for had there not been now a much greater slaughter among the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And they struck the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> that day from Mikhmas <char style="add">[hidden]</char> to Ayalon <char style="add">[Field of Deer]</char>: and the people were very faint.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And the people flew upon the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>, and took sheep, and oxen, and calves, and killed <char style="add">[them]</char> on the ground: and the people did eat <char style="add">[them]</char> with the blood.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />Then they told Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, saying, Behold, the people sin against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, in that they eat with the blood. And he said, You<char style="ord">2f</char> have transgressed: roll a great stone unto me this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said, Disperse yourselves among the people, and say unto them, Bring me here every man his ox, and every man his sheep, and slay <char style="add">[them]</char> here, and eat; and sin not against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in eating with the blood. And all the people brought every man his ox with him that night, and killed <char style="add">[them]</char> there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> built an altar unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: the same was the first altar that he built unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said, Let us go down after the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> by night, and spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> them until the morning light, and let us not leave a man of them. And they said, Do whatsoever seems good unto you<char style="ord">i</char>. Then said the priest, Let us draw near here unto God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> asked counsel of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, Shall I go down after the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>? will you<char style="ord">i</char> deliver them into the hand of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>? But he answered him not that day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said, Draw you<char style="ord">2f</char> near here, all the chief of the people: and know and see wherein this sin has been this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />For, <char style="add">[as]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, which saves Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, though it be in Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> my son, he shall surely die. But <char style="add">[there was]</char> not a man among all the people <char style="add">[that]</char> answered him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />Then said he unto all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Be you<char style="ord">2f</char> on one side, and I and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> my son will be on the other side. And the people said unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, Do what seems good unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />Therefore Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Give a perfect <char style="add">[lot]</char>. And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> were taken: but the people escaped.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said, Cast <char style="add">[lots]</char> between me and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> my son. And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> was taken.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />Then Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said to Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>, Tell me what you<char style="ord">i</char> have done. And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> told him, and said, I did but taste a little honey with the end of the rod that <char style="add">[was]</char> in my hand, <char style="add">[and]</char>, lo, I must die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> answered, God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> do so and more also: for you<char style="ord">i</char> shall surely die, Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />And the people said unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, Shall Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> die, who has wrought this great salvation in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>? God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> forbid: <char style="add">[as]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, there shall not one hair of his head fall to <char style="pn">(to do entirely, do wholly)</char> the ground; for he has wrought with God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> this day. So the people rescued Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>, that he died not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />Then Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> went up from following the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>: and the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> went to their own place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" />So Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> took the kingdom over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and fought against all his enemies on every side, against Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, and against the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and against Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>, and against the kings of Tzovah <char style="add">[station]</char>, and against the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>: and to wherever he turned himself, he vexed <char style="add">[them]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" />And he gathered an host, and struck the ‘Amalekim <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char>, and delivered Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> out of the hands of them that spoiled them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" />Now the sons of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> were Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>, and Yishvi <char style="add">[he resembles me]</char>, and Malkishua <char style="add">[my king is wealth]</char>: and the names of his two daughters <char style="add">[were these]</char>; the name of the firstborn Merav <char style="add">[increase]</char>, and the name of the younger Mikhal <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" />And the name of Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> wife <char style="add">[was]</char> Achino’am <char style="add">[my brother is delight]</char>, the daughter of Achima’atz <char style="add">[my brother is anger (wrath)]</char>: and the name of the captain of his host <char style="add">[was]</char> Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char>, the son of Ner <char style="add">[lamp]</char>, Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> uncle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="51" style="v" />And Kish <char style="add">[bent] [was]</char> the father of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>; and Ner <char style="add">[lamp]</char> the father of Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp] [was]</char> the son of Avi’el <char style="add">[El (God) is my father]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="52" style="v" />And there was sore war against the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> all the days of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>: and when Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> saw any strong man, or any valiant man, he took him unto him.</para>
  <chapter number="15" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> also said unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sent me to anoint you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[to be]</char> king over his people, over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: now therefore hearken you<char style="ord">i</char> unto the voice of the words of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, I remember <char style="add">[that]</char> which ‘Amalek <char style="add">[Dweller in a Valley]</char> did to Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, how he laid <char style="add">[wait]</char> for him in the way, when he came up from Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Now go and strike ‘Amalek <char style="add">[Dweller in a Valley]</char>, and utterly destroy all that they have, and spare them not; but slay both man and woman, infant and suckling, ox and sheep, camel and ass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> gathered the people together, and numbered them in T’la’im <char style="add">[lambs]</char>, two hundred thousand footmen, and ten thousand men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> came to a city of ‘Amalek <char style="add">[Dweller in a Valley]</char>, and laid wait in the valley.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said unto the Keini <char style="add">[traveling tinkers or blacksmiths]</char>, Go, depart, get you down from among the ‘Amalekim <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char>, lest I destroy you with them: for you<char style="ord">2f</char> showed kindness to all the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, when they came up out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>. So the Keini <char style="add">[traveling tinkers or blacksmiths]</char> departed from among the ‘Amalekim <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> struck the ‘Amalekim <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char> from Havilah <char style="pn">(Stretch of Sand)</char> <char style="add">[until]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> come to Shur <char style="add">[wall]</char>, that <char style="add">[is]</char> over against Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And he took Agag <char style="add">[Violent]</char> the king of the ‘Amalekim <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char> alive, and utterly destroyed all the people with the edge of the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />But Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and the people spared Agag <char style="add">[Violent]</char>, and the best of the sheep, and of the oxen, and of the fatlings, and the lambs, and all <char style="add">[that was]</char> good, and would not utterly destroy them: but everything <char style="add">[that was]</char> vile and refuse, that they destroyed utterly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Then came the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> unto Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />It repents me that I have set up Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired] [to be]</char> king: for he is turned back from following me, and has not performed my commandments. And it grieved Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>; and he cried unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> all night.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And when Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> rose early to meet Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> in the morning, it was told Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, saying, Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> came to Carmel <char style="add">[Garden-land]</char>, and, behold, he set him up a place, and is gone about, and passed on, and gone down to Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> came to Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>: and Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said unto him, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: I have performed the commandment of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said, What <char style="add">[means]</char> then this bleating of the sheep in my ears, and the lowing of the oxen which I hear?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said, They have brought them from the ‘Amalekim <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char>: for the people spared the best of the sheep and of the oxen, to sacrifice unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; and the rest we have utterly destroyed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Then Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, Stay, and I will tell you<char style="ord">i</char> what the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has said to me this night. And he said unto him, Say on.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said, When you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[were]</char> little in you<char style="ord">i</char> own sight, <char style="add">[were]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> not <char style="add">[made]</char> the head of the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> anointed you<char style="ord">i</char> king over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sent you<char style="ord">i</char> on a journey, and said, Go and utterly destroy the sinners the ‘Amalekim <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char>, and fight against them until they be consumed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />For what reason then did you<char style="ord">i</char> not obey the voice of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, but did fly upon the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>, and did evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said unto Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, Yes, I have obeyed the voice of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and have gone the way which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sent me, and have brought Agag <char style="add">[Violent]</char> the king of ‘Amalek <char style="add">[Dweller in a Valley]</char>, and have utterly destroyed the ‘Amalekim <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />But the people took of the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>, sheep and oxen, the chief of the things which should have been utterly destroyed, to sacrifice unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> in Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said, Has the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[as great]</char> delight in burnt offerings and sacrifices, as in obeying the voice of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>? Behold, to obey <char style="add">[is]</char> better than sacrifice, <char style="add">[and]</char> to hearken than the fat of rams.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />For rebellion <char style="add">[is as]</char> the sin of witchcraft, and stubbornness <char style="add">[is as]</char> iniquity and idolatry. Because you<char style="ord">i</char> have rejected the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, he has also rejected you<char style="ord">i</char> from <char style="add">[being]</char> king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said unto Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, I have sinned: for I have transgressed the commandment of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> words: because I feared the people, and obeyed their voice.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Now therefore, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, pardon my sin, and turn again with me, that I may worship the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, I will not return with you<char style="ord">i</char>: for you<char style="ord">i</char> have rejected the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has rejected you<char style="ord">i</char> from being king over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And as Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> turned about to go away, he laid hold upon the skirt of his Mantle <char style="pn">(cloak; covering garment)</char> <char style="pn">(cloak)</char>, and it rent.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said unto him, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has rent the kingdom of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> from you<char style="ord">i</char> this day, and has given it to a neighbour of you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[that is]</char> better than you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And also the Strength of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> will not lie nor repent: for he <char style="add">[is]</char> not a man, that he should repent.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Then he said, I have sinned: <char style="add">[yet]</char> honour me now, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, before the elders of my people, and before Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and turn again with me, that I may worship the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />So Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> turned again after Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>; and Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> worshipped the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />Then said Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, Bring you<char style="ord">2f</char> here to me Agag <char style="add">[Violent]</char> the king of the ‘Amalekim <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char>. And Agag <char style="add">[Violent]</char> came unto him delicately. And Agag <char style="add">[Violent]</char> said, Surely the bitterness of death is past.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said, As you<char style="ord">i</char> sword has made women childless, so shall you<char style="ord">i</char> mother be childless among women. And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> hewed Agag <char style="add">[Violent]</char> in pieces before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />Then Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> went to Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>; and Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> went up to his house to Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> came no more to see Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> until the day of his death: nevertheless Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> mourned for Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> repented that he had made Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> king over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="16" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, How long will you<char style="ord">i</char> mourn for Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, seeing I have rejected him from reigning over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>? fill you<char style="ord">i</char> horn with oil, and go, I will send you<char style="ord">i</char> to Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> the Beit-Lachmi <char style="add">[house of bread]</char>: for I have provided me a king among his sons.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said, How can I go? if Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> hear <char style="add">[it]</char>, he will kill me. And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said, Take an heifer with you<char style="ord">i</char>, and say, I am come to sacrifice to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And call Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> to the sacrifice, and I will show you<char style="ord">i</char> what you<char style="ord">i</char> shall do: and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall anoint unto me <char style="add">[him]</char> whom I name unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> did that which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke, and came to Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char>. And the elders of the town trembled at his coming, and said, Come you<char style="ord">i</char> peaceably?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he said, Peaceably: I am come to sacrifice unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> yourselves, and come with me to the sacrifice. And he sanctified Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> and his sons, and called them to the sacrifice.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And it came to pass, when they were come, that he looked on ‘Eli’av <char style="add">[My Father is God]</char>, and said, Surely the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> anointed <char style="add">[is]</char> before him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />But the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, Look not on his Countenance <char style="pn">(Face, appearance; show favor)</char>, or on the height of his stature; because I have refused him: for [the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sees] not as man sees; for man looks on the outward appearance, but the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> looks on the heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> called Avinadav <char style="add">[my father is noble]</char>, and made him pass before Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>. And he said, Neither has the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> chosen this.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> made Shammah <char style="add">[astonishment]</char> to pass by. And he said, Neither has the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> chosen this.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Again, Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> made seven of his sons to pass before Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>. And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said unto Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char>, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has not chosen these.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said unto Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char>, Are here all <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> children? And he said, There remains yet the youngest, and, behold, he keeps the sheep. And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said unto Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char>, Send and fetch him: for we will not sit down till he come here.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And he sent, and brought him in. Now he <char style="add">[was]</char> ruddy <char style="pn">(reddish hair or complexion)</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> withal of a beautiful Countenance <char style="pn">(Face, appearance; show favor)</char>, and goodly to look to. And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said, Arise, anoint him: for this <char style="add">[is]</char> he.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Then Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> took the horn of oil, and anointed him in the midst of his brethren: and the Spirit of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came upon David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> from that day forward. So Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> rose up, and went to Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />But the Spirit of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> departed from Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and an evil spirit from the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> troubled him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> servants said unto him, Behold now, an evil spirit from God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> troubles you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Let our lord now command your<char style="ord">i</char> servants, <char style="add">[which are]</char> before you<char style="ord">i</char>, to seek out a man, <char style="add">[who is]</char> a cunning player on an harp: and it shall come to pass, when the evil spirit from God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> is upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, that he shall play with his hand, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be well.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said unto his servants, Provide me now a man that can play well, and bring <char style="add">[him]</char> to me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then answered one of the servants, and said, Behold, I have seen a son of Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> the Beit-Lachmi <char style="add">[house of bread]</char>, <char style="add">[that is]</char> cunning in playing, and a mighty valiant man, and a man of war, and prudent in matters, and a comely <char style="pn">(attractive; proper (one’s own; peculiar; particular); becoming)</char> person, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />For what reason Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> sent messengers unto Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char>, and said, Send me David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> son, which <char style="add">[is]</char> with the sheep.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> took an ass <char style="add">[laden]</char> with bread, and a bottle of wine, and a kid, and sent <char style="add">[them]</char> by David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his son unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> came to Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and stood before him: and he loved him greatly; and he became his armourbearer.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> sent to Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char>, saying, Let David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, stand before me; for he has found favour in my sight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And it came to pass, when the <char style="add">[evil]</char> spirit from God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> was upon Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> took an harp, and played with his hand: so Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> was refreshed, and was well, and the evil spirit departed from him.</para>
  <chapter number="17" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> gathered together their armies to battle, and were gathered together at Sokhoh <char style="add">[bushy]</char>, which <char style="add">[belongs]</char> to Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and pitched between Sokhoh <char style="add">[bushy]</char> and ‘Azekah <char style="add">[Dug Over]</char>, in Efes-Damim <char style="add">[edge of blood]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> were gathered together, and pitched by the valley of Elah <char style="add">[an oak]</char>, and set the battle in array <char style="pn">(to put on; to clothe)</char> against the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> stood on a mountain on the one side, and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> stood on a mountain on the other side: and <char style="add">[there was]</char> a valley between them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And there went out a champion out of the camp of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, named Golyat <char style="add">[splendor]</char>, of Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>, whose height <char style="add">[was]</char> six cubits and a span.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And <char style="add">[he had]</char> an helmet of brass upon his head, and he <char style="add">[was]</char> armed with a coat of mail; and the weight of the coat <char style="add">[was]</char> five thousand shekels of brass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And <char style="add">[he had]</char> greaves of brass upon his legs, and a target <char style="pn">(small shield; buckler)</char> of brass between his shoulders.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the staff of his spear <char style="add">[was]</char> like a weaver’s beam; and his spear’s head <char style="add">[weighed]</char> six hundred shekels of iron: and one bearing a shield went before him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And he stood and cried unto the armies of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and said unto them, Why are you<char style="ord">2f</char> come out to set <char style="add">[your]</char> battle in array <char style="pn">(to put on; to clothe)</char>? <char style="add">[am]</char> not I a P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> servants to Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>? choose you a man for you, and let him come down to me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />If he be able to fight with me, and to kill me, then will we be your servants: but if I prevail against him, and kill him, then shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> be our servants, and serve us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char> said, I defy the armies of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> this day; give me a man, that we may fight together.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />When Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> heard those words of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>, they were dismayed, and greatly afraid.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Now David <char style="add">[beloved] [was]</char> the son of that Efrat [ashiness: fruitfulness] of Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char> in Y’hudah, whose name <char style="add">[was]</char> Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char>; and he had eight sons: and the man went among men <char style="add">[for]</char> an old man in the days of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the three eldest sons of Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> went <char style="add">[and]</char> followed Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> to the battle: and the names of his three sons that went to the battle <char style="add">[were]</char> ‘Eli’av <char style="add">[My Father is God]</char> the firstborn, and next unto him Avinadav <char style="add">[my father is noble]</char>, and the third Shammah <char style="add">[astonishment]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved] [was]</char> the youngest: and the three eldest followed Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />But David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> went and returned from Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> to feed his father’s sheep at Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char> drew near morning and evening, and presented himself forty days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> said unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his son, Take now for you<char style="ord">i</char> brethren an eifah of this parched <char style="add">[corn]</char>, and these ten loaves, and run to the camp to you<char style="ord">i</char> brethren;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And carry these ten cheeses unto the captain of <char style="add">[their]</char> thousand, and look how you<char style="ord">i</char> brethren fare, and take their pledge.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Now Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and they, and all the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[were]</char> in the valley of Elah <char style="add">[an oak]</char>, fighting with the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> rose up early in the morning, and left the sheep with a keeper, and took, and went, as Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> had commanded him; and he came to the trench, as the host was going forth to the fight, and shouted for the battle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />For Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> had put the battle in array <char style="pn">(to put on; to clothe)</char>, army against army.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> left his carriage <char style="pn">(baggage)</char> in the hand of the keeper of the carriage <char style="pn">(baggage)</char>, and ran into the army, and came and saluted his brethren.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And as he talked with them, behold, there came up the champion, the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char> of Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>, Golyat <char style="add">[splendor]</char> by name, out of the armies of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and spoke according to the same words: and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> heard <char style="add">[them]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And all the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, when they saw the man, fled from him, and were sore afraid.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said, Have you<char style="ord">2f</char> seen this man that is come up? surely to defy Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> is he come up: and it shall be, <char style="add">[that]</char> the man who kills him, the king will enrich him with great riches, and will give him his daughter, and make his father’s house free in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> spoke to the men that stood by him, saying, What shall be done to the man that kills this P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>, and takes away the reproach <char style="pn">(disgrace; shame)</char> from Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>? for who <char style="add">[is]</char> this uncircumcised P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>, that he should defy the armies of the living God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And the people answered him after this manner, saying, So shall it be done to the man that kills him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And ‘Eli’av <char style="add">[My Father is God]</char> his eldest brother heard when he spoke unto the men; and ‘Eli’av <char style="add">[My Father is God]</char>’s anger was kindled against David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and he said, Why came you<char style="ord">i</char> down here? and with whom have you<char style="ord">i</char> left those few sheep in the wilderness? I know you<char style="ord">i</char> pride, and the naughtiness of you<char style="ord">i</char> heart; for you<char style="ord">i</char> are come down that you<char style="ord">i</char> might see the battle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said, What have I now done? <char style="add">[Is there]</char> not a cause?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And he turned from him toward another, and spoke after the same manner: and the people answered him again after the former manner.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And when the words were heard which David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> spoke, they rehearsed <char style="add">[them]</char> before Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>: and he sent for him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said to Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, Let no man’s heart fail because of him; you<char style="ord">i</char> servant will go and fight with this P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> are not able to go against this P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char> to fight with him: for you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are but]</char> a youth, and he a man of war from his youth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, You<char style="ord">1s</char> servant kept his father’s sheep, and there came a lion, and a bear, and took a lamb out of the flock:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And I went out after him, and struck him, and delivered <char style="add">[it]</char> out of his mouth: and when he arose against me, I caught <char style="add">[him]</char> by his beard, and struck him, and killed him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />You<char style="ord">1s</char> servant killed both the lion and the bear: and this uncircumcised P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char> shall be as one of them, seeing he has defied the armies of the living God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said moreover, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> that delivered me out of the paw of the lion, and out of the paw of the bear, he will deliver me out of the hand of this P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>. And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Go, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> be with you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> armed David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> with his armour, and he put an helmet of brass upon his head; also he armed him with a coat of mail.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> girded his sword upon his armour, and he assayed <char style="pn">(attempted; tested; analyzed)</char> to go; for he had not proved <char style="add">[it]</char>. And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, I cannot go with these; for I have not proved <char style="add">[them]</char>. And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> put them off him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />And he took his staff in his hand, and chose him five smooth stones out of the brook, and put them in a shepherd’s bag which he had, even in a scrip; and his sling <char style="add">[was]</char> in his hand: and he drew near to the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char> came on and drew near unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>; and the man that bore the shield <char style="add">[went]</char> before him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />And when the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char> looked about, and saw David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, he disdained him: for he was <char style="add">[but]</char> a youth, and ruddy <char style="pn">(reddish hair or complexion)</char>, and of a fair Countenance <char style="pn">(Face, appearance; show favor)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char> said unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, <char style="add">[Am]</char> I a dog, that you<char style="ord">i</char> come to me with rods (clubs)? And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char> cursed David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> by his gods.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char> said to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Come to me, and I will give you<char style="ord">i</char> flesh unto the fowls of the air, and to the beasts of the field.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />Then said David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> to the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> come to me with a sword, and with a spear, and with a shield: but I come to you<char style="ord">i</char> in the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of the armies of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, whom you<char style="ord">i</char> have defied.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />This day will the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> deliver you<char style="ord">i</char> into my hand; and I will strike you<char style="ord">i</char>, and take you<char style="ord">i</char> head from you<char style="ord">i</char>; and I will give the carcasses of the host of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> this day unto the fowls of the air, and to the wild beasts of the earth; that all the earth may know that there is a God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" />And all this assembly shall know that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> saves not with sword and spear: for the battle <char style="add">[is]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char>, and he will give you into our hands.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" />And it came to pass, when the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char> arose, and came and drew near to meet David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> hasted, and ran toward the army to meet the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> put his hand in his bag, and took there a stone, and slang <char style="add">[it]</char>, and struck the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char> in his forehead, that the stone sunk into his forehead; and he fell upon his face to the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" />So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> prevailed over the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char> with a sling and with a stone, and struck the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>, and killed him; but <char style="add">[there was]</char> no sword in the hand of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="51" style="v" />Therefore David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> ran, and stood upon the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>, and took his sword, and drew it out of the sheath thereof, and killed him, and cut off his head with that. And when the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> saw their champion was dead, they fled.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="52" style="v" />And the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> arose, and shouted, and pursued the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, until you<char style="ord">i</char> come to the valley, and to the gates of ‘Ekron <char style="add">[Torn Up by the Roots]</char>. And the wounded of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> fell down by the way to Sha’arayim <char style="add">[double gate]</char>, even unto Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>, and unto ‘Ekron <char style="add">[Torn Up by the Roots]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="53" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> returned from chasing after the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and they spoiled their tents.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="54" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> took the head of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>, and brought it to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>; but he put his armour in his tent.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="55" style="v" />And when Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> saw David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> go forth against the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>, he said unto Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char>, the captain of the host, Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char>, whose son <char style="add">[is]</char> this youth? And Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> said, <char style="add">[As]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> soul lives, O king, I cannot tell.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="56" style="v" />And the king said, Enquire you<char style="ord">i</char> whose son the stripling <char style="add">[is]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="57" style="v" />And as David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> returned from the slaughter of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>, Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> took him, and brought him before Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> with the head of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char> in his hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="58" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said to him, Whose son <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> young man? And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> answered, I <char style="add">[am]</char> the son of you<char style="ord">i</char> servant Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> the Beit-Lachmi <char style="add">[house of bread]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="18" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass, when he had made an end of speaking unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, that the soul of Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> was knit with the soul of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> loved him as his own soul.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> took him that day, and would let him go no more home to his father’s house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Then Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> made a covenant, because he loved him as his own soul.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> stripped himself of the robe that <char style="add">[was]</char> upon him, and gave it to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and his garments, even to his sword, and to his bow, and to his belt.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> went out to wherever Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> sent him, <char style="add">[and]</char> behaved himself wisely: and Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> set him over the men of war, and he was accepted in the sight of all the people, and also in the sight of Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> servants.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And it came to pass as they came, when David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> was returned from the slaughter of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>, that the women came out of all cities of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, singing and dancing, to meet king Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, with tambourines, with joy, and with instruments of music.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the women answered <char style="add">[one another]</char> as they played, and said, Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> has slain his thousands, and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his ten thousands.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> was very exceedingly angry, and the saying displeased him; nd he said, They have ascribed unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> ten thousands, and to me they have ascribed <char style="add">[but]</char> thousands: and <char style="add">[what]</char> can he have more but the kingdom?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> eyed David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> from that day and forward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And it came to pass on the morrow, that the evil spirit from God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> came upon Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and he prophesied in the midst of the house: and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> played with his hand, as at other times: and <char style="add">[there was]</char> a javelin in Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> cast the javelin; for he said, I will strike David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> even to the wall <char style="add">[with it]</char>. And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> avoided out of his presence twice.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> was afraid of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, because the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was with him, and was departed from Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Therefore Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> removed him from him, and made him his captain over a thousand; and he went out and came in before the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> behaved himself wisely in all his ways; and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[was]</char> with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />For what reason when Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> saw that he behaved himself very wisely, he was afraid of him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />But all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> loved David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, because he went out and came in before them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Behold my elder daughter Merav <char style="add">[increase]</char>, her will I give you<char style="ord">i</char> to wife: only be you<char style="ord">i</char> valiant for me, and fight the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> battles. For Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said, Let not my hand be upon him, but let the hand of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> be upon him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, Who <char style="add">[am]</char> I? and what <char style="add">[is]</char> my life, <char style="add">[or]</char> my father’s family in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that I should be son in law to the king?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />But it came to pass at the time when Merav <char style="add">[increase]</char> Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> daughter should have been given to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, that she was given unto Adri’el <char style="add">[flock of God]</char> the Mecholati <char style="add">[dancing (in sadness)]</char> to wife.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Mikhal <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> daughter loved David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: and they told Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and the thing pleased him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said, I will give him her, that she may be a snare to him, and that the hand of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> may be against him. For what reason Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall this day be my son in law in <char style="add">[the one of]</char> the two.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> commanded his servants, <char style="add">[saying]</char>, Commune with David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> secretly, and say, Behold, the king has delight in you<char style="ord">i</char>, and all his servants love you<char style="ord">i</char>: now therefore be the king’s son in law.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> servants spoke those words in the ears of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>. And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said, Seem it to you <char style="add">[a]</char> light <char style="add">[thing]</char> to be a king’s son in law, seeing that I <char style="add">[am]</char> a poor man, and lightly esteemed?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the servants of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> told him, saying, On this manner spoke David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said, Thus shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> say to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, The king desires not any dowry, but an hundred foreskins of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, to be avenged of the king’s enemies. But Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> thought to make David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> fall by the hand of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And when his servants told David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> these words, it pleased David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> well to be the king’s son in law: and the days were not expired.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />For what reason David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> arose and went, he and his men, and killed of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> two hundred men; and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> brought their foreskins, and they gave them in full tale to the king, that he might be the king’s son in law. And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> gave him Mikhal <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> his daughter to wife.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> saw and knew that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[was]</char> with David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and <char style="add">[that]</char> Mikhal <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> daughter loved him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> was yet the more afraid of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>; and Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> became David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s enemy continually.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Then the princes of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> went forth: and it came to pass, after they went forth, <char style="add">[that]</char> David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> behaved himself more wisely than all the servants of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>; so that his name was much set by.</para>
  <chapter number="19" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> spoke to Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> his son, and to all his servants, that they should kill David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />But Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> son delighted much in David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> told David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, saying, Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> my father seeks to kill you<char style="ord">i</char>: now therefore, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, take heed to yourself until the morning, and abide in a secret <char style="add">[place]</char>, and hide yourself:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And I will go out and stand beside my father in the field where you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char>, and I will commune with my father of you<char style="ord">i</char>; and what I see, that I will tell you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> spoke good of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> his father, and said unto him, Let not the king sin against his servant, against David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>; because he has not sinned against you<char style="ord">i</char>, and because his works <char style="add">[have been]</char> to you<char style="ord">i</char>-ward <char style="pn">(in custody, with a guard; prison)</char> very good:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />For he did put his life in his hand, and killed the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> wrought a great salvation for all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: you<char style="ord">i</char> saw <char style="add">[it]</char>, and did rejoice: wherefore then will you<char style="ord">i</char> sin against innocent blood, to slay David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> without a cause?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> listened unto the voice of Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>: and Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> swore, <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, he shall not be slain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> called David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> showed him all those things. And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> brought David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> to Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and he was in his presence, as in times past.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And there was war again: and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> went out, and fought with the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and killed them with a great slaughter; and they fled from him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the evil spirit from the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was upon Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, as he sat in his house with his javelin in his hand: and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> played with <char style="add">[his]</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> sought to strike David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> even to the wall with the javelin; but he slipped away out of Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> presence, and he struck the javelin into the wall: and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> fled, and escaped that night.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> also sent messengers unto David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s house, to watch him, and to slay him in the morning: and Mikhal <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s wife told him, saying, If you<char style="ord">i</char> save not you<char style="ord">i</char> life tonight, tomorrow you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be slain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />So Mikhal <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> let David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> down through a window: and he went, and fled, and escaped.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Mikhal <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> took an image, and laid <char style="add">[it]</char> in the bed, and put a pillow of goats’ <char style="add">[hair]</char> for his bolster <char style="pn">(pillow; head - or other - support)</char>, and covered <char style="add">[it]</char> with a cloth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And when Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> sent messengers to take David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, she said, He <char style="add">[is]</char> sick.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> sent the messengers <char style="add">[again]</char> to see David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, saying, Bring him up to me in the bed, that I may slay him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And when the messengers were come in, behold, <char style="add">[there was]</char> an image in the bed, with a pillow of goats’ <char style="add">[hair]</char> for his bolster <char style="pn">(pillow; head - or other - support)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said unto Mikhal <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char>, Why have you<char style="ord">i</char> deceived me so, and sent away my enemy, that he is escaped? And Mikhal <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> answered Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, He said unto me, Let me go; why should I kill you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> fled, and escaped, and came to Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> to Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, and told him all that Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> had done to him. And he and Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> went and dwelt in Nayot <char style="add">[the prophet’s dormitory]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And it was told Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, saying, Behold, David <char style="add">[beloved] [is]</char> at Nayot <char style="add">[the prophet’s dormitory]</char> in Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> sent messengers to take David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: and when they saw the company of the prophets prophesying, and Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> standing <char style="add">[as]</char> appointed over them, the Spirit of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> was upon the messengers of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and they also prophesied.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And when it was told Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, he sent other messengers, and they prophesied likewise. And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> sent messengers again the third time, and they prophesied also.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Then went he also to Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, and came to a great well that <char style="add">[is]</char> in Sekhu <char style="add">[the watch-tower]</char>: and he asked and said, Where <char style="add">[are]</char> Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>? And <char style="add">[one]</char> said, Behold, <char style="add">[they be]</char> at Nayot <char style="add">[the prophet’s dormitory]</char> in Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And he went there to Nayot <char style="add">[the prophet’s dormitory]</char> in Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>: and the Spirit of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> was upon him also, and he went on, and prophesied, until he came to Nayot <char style="add">[the prophet’s dormitory]</char> in Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And he stripped off his clothes also, and prophesied before Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> in like manner, and lay down naked all that day and all that night. For this reason they say, <char style="add">[Is]</char> Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> also among the prophets?</para>
  <chapter number="20" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> fled from Nayot <char style="add">[the prophet’s dormitory]</char> in Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, and came and said before Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>, What have I done? what <char style="add">[is]</char> my iniquity? and what <char style="add">[is]</char> my sin before you<char style="ord">i</char> father, that he seeks my life?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he said unto him, God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> forbid; you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not die: behold, my father will do nothing either great or small, but that he will show it me: and why should my father hide this thing from me? it <char style="add">[is]</char> not <char style="add">[so]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> swore moreover, and said, You<char style="ord">1s</char> father certainly knows that I have found grace in you<char style="ord">i</char> eyes; and he says, Let not Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> know this, lest he be grieved: but truly <char style="add">[as]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, and <char style="add">[as]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> soul lives, <char style="add">[there is]</char> but a step between me and death.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then said Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Whatsoever you<char style="ord">i</char> soul desires, I will even do <char style="add">[it]</char> for you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>, Behold, tomorrow <char style="add">[is]</char> the new moon, and I should not fail to sit with the king at meat: but let me go, that I may hide myself in the field unto the third <char style="add">[day]</char> at even.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />If you<char style="ord">i</char> father at all miss me, then say, David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> earnestly asked <char style="add">[leave]</char> of me that he might run to Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char> his city: for <char style="add">[there is]</char> a yearly sacrifice there for all the family.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />If he say thus, <char style="add">[It is]</char> well; your<char style="ord">i</char> servant shall have peace: but if he be very exceedingly angry, <char style="add">[then]</char> be sure that evil is determined by him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Therefore you<char style="ord">i</char> shall deal kindly with your<char style="ord">i</char> servant; for you<char style="ord">i</char> have brought your<char style="ord">i</char> servant into a covenant of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char>: notwithstanding, if there be in me iniquity, slay me yourself; for why should you<char style="ord">i</char> bring me to your<char style="ord">i</char> father?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> said, Far be it from you<char style="ord">i</char>: for if I knew certainly that evil were determined by my father to come upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, then would not I tell it you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Then said David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> to Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>, Who shall tell me? or what <char style="add">[if]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> father answer you<char style="ord">i</char> roughly?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> said unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Come, and let us go out into the field. And they went out both of them into the field.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> said unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, when I have sounded my father about tomorrow any time, <char style="add">[or]</char> the third <char style="add">[day]</char>, and, behold, <char style="add">[if there be]</char> good toward David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and I then send not unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, and show it you<char style="ord">i</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> do so and much more to Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>: but if it please my father <char style="add">[to do]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> evil, then I will show it you<char style="ord">i</char>, and send you<char style="ord">i</char> away, that you<char style="ord">i</char> may go in peace: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> be with you<char style="ord">i</char>, as he has been with my father.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not only while yet I live show me the kindness of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that I die not:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />But <char style="add">[also]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not cut off you<char style="ord">i</char> kindness from my house forever: no, not when the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has cut off the enemies of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> everyone from the face of the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />So Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> made <char style="add">[a covenant]</char> with the house of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, <char style="add">[saying]</char>, Let the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> even require <char style="add">[it]</char> at the hand of David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s enemies.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> caused David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> to swear again, because he loved him: for he loved him as he loved his own soul.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> said to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Tomorrow <char style="add">[is]</char> the new moon: and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be missed, because you<char style="ord">i</char> seat will be empty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And <char style="add">[when]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> have detained <char style="pn">(held)</char> three days, <char style="add">[then]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> shall go down quickly, and come to the place where you<char style="ord">i</char> did hide yourself when the business was <char style="add">[in hand]</char>, and shall remain by the stone Ezel <char style="add">[departure]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And I will shoot three arrows on the side <char style="add">[thereof]</char>, as though I shot at a mark.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And, behold, I will send a boy, <char style="add">[saying]</char>, Go, find out the arrows. If I expressly say unto the boy, Behold, the arrows <char style="add">[are]</char> on this side of you<char style="ord">i</char>, take them; then come you<char style="ord">i</char>: for <char style="add">[there is]</char> peace to you<char style="ord">i</char>, and no hurt; <char style="add">[as]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />But if I say thus unto the young man, Behold, the arrows <char style="add">[are]</char> beyond you<char style="ord">i</char>; go you<char style="ord">i</char> way: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has sent you<char style="ord">i</char> away.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And <char style="add">[as touching]</char> the matter which you<char style="ord">i</char> and I have spoken of, behold, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> between you<char style="ord">i</char> and me forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> hid himself in the field: and when the new moon was come, the king sat him down to eat meat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And the king sat upon his seat, as at other times, <char style="add">[even]</char> upon a seat by the wall: and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> arose, and Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> sat by Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> side, and David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s place was empty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Nevertheless Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> spoke not anything that day: for he thought, Something has befallen him, he <char style="add">[is]</char> not clean; surely he <char style="add">[is]</char> not clean.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And it came to pass on the morrow, <char style="add">[which was]</char> the second <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, that David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s place was empty: and Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said unto Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> his son, For what reason comes not the son of Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> to meat, neither yesterday, nor to day?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> answered Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> earnestly asked <char style="add">[leave]</char> of me <char style="add">[to go]</char> to Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And he said, Let me go, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>; for our family has a sacrifice in the city; and my brother, he has commanded me <char style="add">[to be there]</char>: and now, if I have found favour in you<char style="ord">i</char> eyes, let me get away, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, and see my brethren. Therefore he comes not unto the king’s table.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Then Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> anger was kindled against Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>, and he said unto him, you<char style="ord">i</char> son of the perverse rebellious <char style="add">[woman]</char>, do not I know that you<char style="ord">i</char> have chosen the son of Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> to you<char style="ord">i</char> own confusion, and unto the confusion of you<char style="ord">i</char> mother’s nakedness?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />For as long as the son of Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> lives upon the ground, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not be established, nor you<char style="ord">i</char> kingdom. For what reason now send and fetch him unto me, for he shall surely die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> answered Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> his father, and said unto him, For what reason shall he be slain? what has he done?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> cast a javelin at him to strike him: whereby Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> knew that it was determined of his father to slay David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />So Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> arose from the table in fierce anger, and did eat no meat the second day of the month: for he was grieved for David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, because his father had done him shame.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And it came to pass in the morning, that Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> went out into the field at the time appointed with David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and a little boy with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And he said unto his boy, Run, find out now the arrows which I shoot. <char style="add">[And]</char> as the boy ran, he shot an arrow beyond him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And when the boy was come to the place of the arrow which Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> had shot, Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> cried after the boy, and said, <char style="add">[Is]</char> not the arrow beyond you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> cried after the boy, Make speed, haste, stay not. And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>’s boy gathered up the arrows, and came to his master.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />But the boy knew not anything: only Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> knew the matter.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> gave his artillery unto his boy, and said unto him, Go, carry <char style="add">[them]</char> to the city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[And]</char> as soon as the boy was gone, David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> arose out of <char style="add">[a place]</char> toward the south, and fell on his face to the ground, and bowed himself three times: and they kissed one another, and wept one with another, until David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> exceeded.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> said to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Go in peace, forasmuch as we have sworn both of us in the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> be between me and you<char style="ord">i</char>, and between my seed and you<char style="ord">i</char> seed forever. And he arose and departed: and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> went into the city.</para>
  <chapter number="21" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then came David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> to Nov <char style="add">[high place]</char> to Achi-Melekh <char style="add">[my brother is king]</char> the priest: and Achi-Melekh <char style="add">[my brother is king]</char> was afraid at the meeting of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and said unto him, Why <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> alone, and no man with you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto Achi-Melekh <char style="add">[my brother is king]</char> the priest, The king has commanded me a business, and has said unto me, Let no man know anything of the business about which I send you<char style="ord">i</char>, and what I have commanded you<char style="ord">i</char>: and I have appointed <char style="add">[my]</char> servants to such and such a place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Now therefore what is under you<char style="ord">i</char> hand? give <char style="add">[me]</char> five <char style="add">[loaves of]</char> bread in my hand, or what there is present.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the priest answered David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and said, <char style="add">[There is]</char> no common bread under my hand, but there is consecrated bread; if the young men have kept themselves at least from women.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> answered the priest, and said unto him, Of a twomen <char style="add">[have been]</char> kept from us about these three days, since I came out, and the vessels of the young men are holy, and <char style="add">[the bread is]</char> in a manner common, yes, though it were sanctified this day in the vessel.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />So the priest gave him consecrated <char style="add">[bread]</char>: for there was no bread there but the showbread, that was taken from before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, to put hot bread in the day when it was taken away.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Now a certain man of the servants of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired] [was]</char> there that day, detained before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and his name <char style="add">[was]</char> Do’eg <char style="add">[fearing]</char>, an Edomi <char style="add">[red]</char>, the most important of the herdsmen that <char style="add">[belonged]</char> to Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto Achi-Melekh <char style="add">[my brother is king]</char>, And is there not here under you<char style="ord">i</char> hand spear or sword? for I have neither brought my sword nor my weapons with me, because the king’s business required haste.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the priest said, The sword of Golyat <char style="add">[splendor]</char> the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>, whom you<char style="ord">i</char> killed in the valley of Elah <char style="add">[an oak]</char>, behold, it <char style="add">[is here]</char> wrapped in a cloth behind the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>: if you<char style="ord">i</char> will take that, take <char style="add">[it]</char>: for <char style="add">[there is]</char> no other save that here. And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said, <char style="add">[There is]</char> none like that; give it me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> arose, and fled that day for fear of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and went to Akhish [meaning disputed; I will blacken <char style="pn">(or terrify)</char> or only a man] the king of Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the servants of Akhish <char style="add">[meaning disputed; I will blacken (or terrify) or only a man]</char> said unto him, <char style="add">[Is]</char> not this David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> the king of the land? did they not sing one to another of him in dances, saying, Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> has slain his thousands, and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his ten thousands?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> laid up these words in his heart, and was sore afraid of Akhish [meaning disputed; I will blacken <char style="pn">(or terrify)</char> or only a man] the king of Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he changed his behaviour before them, and feigned himself mad in their hands, and scrabbled on the doors of the gate, and let his spittle fall down upon his beard.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then said Akhish [meaning disputed; I will blacken <char style="pn">(or terrify)</char> or only a man] unto his servants, Lo, you<char style="ord">2f</char> see the man is mad: wherefore <char style="add">[then]</char> have you<char style="ord">2f</char> brought him to me?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Have I need of mad men, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> have brought this <char style="add">[fellow]</char> to play the mad man in my presence? shall this <char style="add">[fellow]</char> come into my house?</para>
  <chapter number="22" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> therefore departed there, and escaped to the cave ‘Adulam <char style="add">[Justice of the People]</char>: and when his brethren and all his father’s house heard <char style="add">[it]</char>, they went down there to him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And everyone <char style="add">[that was]</char> in distress, and everyone that <char style="add">[was]</char> in debt, and everyone <char style="add">[that was]</char> discontented, gathered themselves unto him; and he became a captain over them: and there were with him about four hundred men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> went there to Mitzpah <char style="add">[Watchtower]</char> of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>: and he said unto the king of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, Let my father and my mother, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, come forth, <char style="add">[and be]</char> with you, till I know what God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> will do for me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he brought them before the king of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>: and they dwelt with him all the while that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> was in the hold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the prophet Gad <char style="add">[Good Fortune with Troublesome Effort]</char> said unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Abide not in the hold; depart, and get you<char style="ord">i</char> into the land of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>. Then David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> departed, and came into the forest of Haret <char style="add">[forest]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />When Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> heard that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> was discovered, and the men that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him, (now Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> abode in Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> under a tree in Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, having his spear in his hand, and all his servants <char style="add">[were]</char> standing about him;)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Then Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said unto his servants that stood about him, Hear now, you<char style="ord">2f</char> Binyamini; will the son of Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> give everyone of you fields and vineyards, <char style="add">[and]</char> make you all captains of thousands, and captains of hundreds;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />That all of you have conspired against me, and <char style="add">[there is]</char> none that shows me that my son has made a league with the son of Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char>, and <char style="add">[there is]</char> none of you that is sorry for me, or shows unto me that my son has stirred up my servant against me, to lie in wait, as at this day?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then answered Do’eg <char style="add">[fearing]</char> the Edomi <char style="add">[red]</char>, which was set over the servants of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and said, I saw the son of Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> coming to Nov <char style="add">[high place]</char>, to Achi-Melekh <char style="add">[my brother is king]</char> the son of Achituv <char style="add">[my brother is good]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And he enquired of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> for him, and gave him victuals <char style="pn">(food for humans)</char>, and gave him the sword of Golyat <char style="add">[splendor]</char> the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Then the king sent to call Achi-Melekh <char style="add">[my brother is king]</char> the priest, the son of Achituv <char style="add">[my brother is good]</char>, and all his father’s house, the priests that <char style="add">[were]</char> in Nov <char style="add">[high place]</char>: and they came all of them to the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said, Hear now, you<char style="ord">i</char> son of Achituv <char style="add">[my brother is good]</char>. And he answered, Here I <char style="add">[am]</char>, my lord.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said unto him, Why have you<char style="ord">2f</char> conspired against me, you<char style="ord">i</char> and the son of Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char>, in that you<char style="ord">i</char> have given him bread, and a sword, and have enquired of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> for him, that he should rise against me, to lie in wait, as at this day?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then Achi-Melekh <char style="add">[my brother is king]</char> answered the king, and said, And who <char style="add">[is so]</char> faithful among all your<char style="ord">i</char> servants as David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, which is the king’s son in law, and goes at you<char style="ord">i</char> bidding, and is honourable in your<char style="ord">i</char> house?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Did I then begin to enquire of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> for him? be it far from me: let not the king impiute <char style="pn">(charge to one’s account; reckon)</char> <char style="add">[any]</char> thing unto his servant, <char style="add">[nor]</char> to all the house of my father: for you<char style="ord">i</char> servant knew nothing of all this, less or more.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the king said, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall surely die, Achi-Melekh <char style="add">[my brother is king]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char>, and all your<char style="ord">i</char> father’s house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the king said unto the footmen that stood about him, Turn, and slay the priests of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; because their hand also <char style="add">[is]</char> with David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and because they knew when he fled, and did not show it to me. But the servants of the king would not put forth their hand to fall upon the priests of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the king said to Do’eg <char style="add">[fearing]</char>, Turn you<char style="ord">i</char>, and fall upon the priests. And Do’eg <char style="add">[fearing]</char> the Edomi <char style="add">[red]</char> turned, and he fell upon the priests, and killed on that day eighty and five persons that did wear a linen ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And Nov <char style="add">[high place]</char>, the city of the priests, struck he with the edge of the sword, both men and women, children and sucklings, and oxen, and asses, and sheep, with the edge of the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And one of the sons of Achi-Melekh <char style="add">[my brother is king]</char> the son of Achituv <char style="add">[my brother is good]</char>, named Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char>, escaped, and fled after David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char> showed David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> that Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> had slain the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> priests.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char>, I knew <char style="add">[it]</char> that day, when Do’eg <char style="add">[fearing]</char> the Edomi <char style="add">[red] [was]</char> there, that he would surely tell Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>: I have occasioned <char style="add">[the death]</char> of all the persons of you<char style="ord">i</char> father’s house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Abide you<char style="ord">i</char> with me, fear not: for he that seeks my life seeks you<char style="ord">i</char> life: but with me you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[shall be]</char> in safeguard.</para>
  <chapter number="23" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then they told David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, saying, Behold, the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> fight against Ke’ilah <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>, and they rob the threshing floors.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Therefore David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> enquired of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, Shall I go and strike these P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>? And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Go, and strike the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and save Ke’ilah <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s men said unto him, Behold, we be afraid here in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>: how much more then if we come to Ke’ilah <char style="add">[Fortress]</char> against the armies of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> enquired of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> yet again. And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> answered him and said, Arise, go down to Ke’ilah <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>; for I will deliver the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> into you<char style="ord">i</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and his men went to Ke’ilah <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>, and fought with the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and brought away their cattle, and struck them with a great slaughter. So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> saved the inhabitants of Ke’ilah <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char> the son of Achi-Melekh <char style="add">[my brother is king]</char> fled to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> to Ke’ilah <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>, <char style="add">[that]</char> he came down <char style="add">[with]</char> an ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char> in his hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And it was told Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> was come to Ke’ilah <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>. And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said, God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> has delivered him into my hand; for he is shut in, by entering into a town that has gates and bars.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> called all the people together to war, to go down to Ke’ilah <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>, to besiege David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and his men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> knew that Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> secretly practiced mischief against him; and he said to Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char> the priest, Bring here the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Then said David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> servant has certainly heard that Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> seeks to come to Ke’ilah <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>, to destroy the city for my sake.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Will the men of Ke’ilah <char style="add">[Fortress]</char> deliver me up into his hand? will Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> come down, as your<char style="ord">i</char> servant has heard? O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, I beseech <char style="pn">(to call upon; appeal; beg)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, tell your<char style="ord">i</char> servant. And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said, He will come down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Then said David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Will the men of Ke’ilah <char style="add">[Fortress]</char> deliver me and my men into the hand of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>? And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said, They will deliver <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Then David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and his men, <char style="add">[which were]</char> about six hundred, arose and departed out of Ke’ilah <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>, and went to wherever they could go. And it was told Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> was escaped from Ke’ilah <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>; and he forbare to go forth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> abode in the wilderness in strong holds, and remained in a mountain in the wilderness of Ziv <char style="add">[brightness]</char> [Battlement (low wall around a roof; wall for defense)]. And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> sought him every day, but God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> delivered him not into his hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> saw that Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> was come out to seek his life: and David <char style="add">[beloved] [was]</char> in the wilderness of Ziv <char style="add">[brightness] [Battlement (low wall around a roof; wall for defense)]</char> in a wood.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> son arose, and went to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> into the wood, and strengthened his hand in God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And he said unto him, Fear not: for the hand of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> my father shall not find you<char style="ord">i</char>; and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be king over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and I shall be next unto you<char style="ord">i</char>; and that also Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> my father knows.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And they two made a covenant before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> abode in the wood, and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> went to his house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Then came up the Zifim <char style="add">[smelters]</char> to Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> to Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, saying, Does not David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> hide himself with us in strong holds in the wood, in the hill of Hikhilah <char style="add">[dark]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> on the south of Y’shim’on <char style="add">[Wasteland]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Now therefore, O king, come down according to all the desire of you<char style="ord">i</char> soul to come down; and our part <char style="add">[shall be]</char> to deliver him into the king’s hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char> of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; for you<char style="ord">2f</char> have compassion on me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Go, I pray you, prepare yet, and know and see his place where his haunt <char style="pn">(where one goes freequently)</char> is, <char style="add">[and]</char> who has seen him there: for it is told me <char style="add">[that]</char> he deals very subtly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />See therefore, and take knowledge of all the lurking places where he hides himself, and come you<char style="ord">2f</char> again to me with the certainty, and I will go with you: and it shall come to pass, if he be in the land, that I will search him out throughout all the thousands of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And they arose, and went to Ziv <char style="add">[brightness] [Battlement (low wall around a roof; wall for defense)]</char> before Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>: but David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and his men <char style="add">[were]</char> in the wilderness of Ma’on <char style="add">[Habitation]</char>, in the plain on the south of Y’shim’on <char style="add">[Wasteland]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> also and his men went to seek <char style="add">[him]</char>. And they told David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: wherefore he came down into a rock, and abode in the wilderness of Ma’on <char style="add">[Habitation]</char>. And when Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> heard <char style="add">[that]</char>, he pursued after David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> in the wilderness of Ma’on <char style="add">[Habitation]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> went on this side of the mountain, and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and his men on that side of the mountain: and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> made haste to get away for fear of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>; for Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and his men compassed David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and his men round about to take them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />But there came a messenger unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, saying, Haste you<char style="ord">i</char>, and come; for the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> have invaded the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />For what reason Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> returned from pursuing after David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and went against the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>: therefore they called that place Sela <char style="add">[the rocks]</char> -Hamachlekot <char style="add">[the cliff of escapes, or divisions]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> went up from there, and dwelt in strong holds at ‘Ein-Gedi <char style="add">[Fount of the Kid]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="24" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> was returned from following the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, that it was told him, saying, Behold, David <char style="add">[beloved] [is]</char> in the wilderness of ‘Ein-Gedi <char style="add">[Fount of the Kid]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Then Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> took three thousand chosen men out of all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and went to seek David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and his men upon the rocks of the wild goats.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he came to the sheepcotes by the way, where <char style="add">[was]</char> a cave; and Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> went in to cover his feet: and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and his men remained in the sides of the cave.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the men of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto him, Behold the day of which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, Behold, I will deliver you<char style="ord">i</char> enemy into you<char style="ord">i</char> hand, that you<char style="ord">i</char> may do to him as it shall seem good unto you<char style="ord">i</char>. Then David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> arose, and cut off the skirt of Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> robe privately.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And it came to pass afterward, that David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s heart struck him, because he had cut off Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> skirt.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he said unto his men, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> forbid that I should do this thing unto my master, the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> anointed, to stretch forth my hand against him, seeing he <char style="add">[is]</char> the anointed of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> detained <char style="pn">(held)</char> his servants with these words, and suffered them not to rise against Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>. But Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> rose up out of the cave, and went on <char style="add">[his]</char> way.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> also arose afterward, and went out of the cave, and cried after Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, saying, My lord the king. And when Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> looked behind him, David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> stooped with his face to the earth, and bowed himself.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said to Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, For what reason hear you<char style="ord">i</char> men’s words, saying, Behold, David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> seeks you<char style="ord">i</char> hurt?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Behold, this day you<char style="ord">i</char> eyes have seen how that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had delivered you<char style="ord">i</char> to day into my hand in the cave: and <char style="add">[some]</char> bade <char style="add">[me]</char> kill you<char style="ord">i</char>: but <char style="add">[my eye]</char> spared you<char style="ord">i</char>; and I said, I will not put forth my hand against my lord; for he <char style="add">[is]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> anointed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Moreover, my father, see, yes, see the skirt of you<char style="ord">i</char> robe in my hand: for in that I cut off the skirt of you<char style="ord">i</char> robe, and killed you<char style="ord">i</char> not, know you<char style="ord">i</char> and see that <char style="add">[there is]</char> neither evil nor transgression in my hand, and I have not sinned against you<char style="ord">i</char>; yet you<char style="ord">i</char> hunt my soul to take it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> judge between me and you<char style="ord">i</char>, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> avenge me of you<char style="ord">i</char>: but my hand shall not be upon you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />As says the proverb of the ancients, Wickedness proceeds from the wicked: but my hand shall not be upon you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />After whom is the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> come out? after whom do you<char style="ord">i</char> pursue? after a dead dog, after a flea.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> therefore be judge, and judge between me and you<char style="ord">i</char>, and see, and plead my cause, and deliver me out of you<char style="ord">i</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And it came to pass, when David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> had made an end of speaking these words unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, that Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said, <char style="add">[Is]</char> this you<char style="ord">i</char> voice, my son David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>? And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> lifted up his voice, and wept.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And he said to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> more righteous than I: for you<char style="ord">i</char> have rewarded me good, whereas I have rewarded you<char style="ord">i</char> evil.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> have showed this day how that you<char style="ord">i</char> have dealt well with me: forasmuch as when the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had delivered me into you<char style="ord">i</char> hand, you<char style="ord">i</char> killed me not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />For if a man find his enemy, will he let him go well away? wherefore the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> reward you<char style="ord">i</char> good for that you<char style="ord">i</char> have done unto me this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And now, behold, I know well that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall surely be king, and that the kingdom of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall be established in your<char style="ord">i</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Swear now therefore unto me by the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that you<char style="ord">i</char> will not cut off my seed after me, and that you<char style="ord">i</char> will not destroy my name out of my father’s house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> swore unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>. And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> went home; but David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and his men got them up unto the hold.</para>
  <chapter number="25" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> died; and all the Yisra’eli’s were gathered together, and lamented him, and buried him in his house at Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>. And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> arose, and went down to the wilderness of Pa’ran <char style="add">[place of caverns]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And <char style="add">[there was]</char> a man in Ma’on <char style="add">[Habitation]</char>, whose possessions <char style="add">[were]</char> in Carmel <char style="add">[Garden-land]</char>; and the man <char style="add">[was]</char> very great, and he had three thousand sheep, and a thousand goats: and he was shearing his sheep in Carmel <char style="add">[Garden-land]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Now the name of the man <char style="add">[was]</char> Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char>; and the name of his wife Avigayil <char style="add">[my father is joy]</char>: and <char style="add">[she was]</char> a woman of good understanding, and of a beautiful Countenance (Face, appearance; show favor): but the man <char style="add">[was]</char> churlish and evil in his doings; and he <char style="add">[was]</char> of the house of Kalev <char style="add">[Dog]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> heard in the wilderness that Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char> did shear his sheep.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> sent out ten young men, and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto the young men, Get you up to Carmel <char style="add">[Garden-land]</char>, and go to Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char>, and greet him in my name:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And thus shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> say to him that lives <char style="add">[in prosperity]</char>, Peace <char style="add">[be]</char> both to you<char style="ord">i</char>, and peace <char style="add">[be]</char> to your<char style="ord">i</char> house, and peace <char style="add">[be]</char> unto all that you<char style="ord">i</char> have.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And now I have heard that you<char style="ord">i</char> have shearers: now your<char style="ord">i</char> shepherds which were with us, we hurt them not, neither was there ought missing unto them, all the while they were in Carmel <char style="add">[Garden-land]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Ask you<char style="ord">i</char> young men, and they will show you<char style="ord">i</char>. For what reason let the young men find favour in you<char style="ord">i</char> eyes: for we come in a good day: give, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, whatsoever comes to your<char style="ord">i</char> hand unto your<char style="ord">i</char> servants, and to your<char style="ord">i</char> son David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And when David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s young men came, they spoke to Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char> according to all those words in the name of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and ceased.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char> answered David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s servants, and said, Who <char style="add">[is]</char> David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>? and who <char style="add">[is]</char> the son of Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char>? there be many servants now a days that break away every man from his master.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Shall I then take my bread, and my water, and my flesh that I have killed for my shearers, and give <char style="add">[it]</char> unto men, whom I know not from what place they <char style="add">[be]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />So David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s young men turned their way, and went again, and came and told him all those sayings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto his men, Gird you<char style="ord">2f</char> on every man his sword. And they girded on every man his sword; and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> also girded on his sword: and there went up after David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> about four hundred men; and two hundred abode by the stuff.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />But one of the young men told Avigayil <char style="add">[my father is joy]</char>, Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char>’s wife, saying, Behold, David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> sent messengers out of the wilderness to salute our master; and he railed on them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />But the men <char style="add">[were]</char> very good unto us, and we were not hurt, neither missed we anything, as long as we were conversant with them, when we were in the fields:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />They were a wall unto us both by night and day, all the while we were with them keeping the sheep.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Now therefore know and consider what you<char style="ord">i</char> will do; for evil is determined against our master, and against all his household: for he <char style="add">[is such]</char> a son of Belial <char style="add">[Worthless, Good for Nothing]</char>, that <char style="add">[a man]</char> cannot speak to him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then Avigayil <char style="add">[my father is joy]</char> made haste, and took two hundred loaves, and two bottles of wine, and five sheep ready dressed, and five measures of parched <char style="add">[corn]</char>, and an hundred clusters of raisins, and two hundred cakes of figs, and laid <char style="add">[them]</char> on asses.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And she said unto her servants, Go on before me; behold, I come after you. But she told not her husband Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And it was <char style="add">[so, as]</char> she rode on the ass, that she came down by the colonnade of the hill, and, behold, David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and his men came down against her; and she met them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Now David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> had said, Surely in vain have I kept all that this <char style="add">[fellow]</char> has in the wilderness, so that nothing was missed of all that <char style="add">[pertained]</char> unto him: and he has requited me evil for good.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />So and more also do God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> unto the enemies of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, if I leave of all that <char style="add">[pertain]</char> to him by the morning light any that pisses against the wall.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And when Avigayil <char style="add">[my father is joy]</char> saw David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, she hasted, and lighted off the ass, and fell before David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> on her face, and bowed herself to the ground,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And fell at his feet, and said, Upon me, my lord, <char style="add">[upon]</char> me <char style="add">[let this]</char> iniquity <char style="add">[be]</char>: and let you<char style="ord">i</char> female servant, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, speak in you<char style="ord">i</char> audience, and hear the words of you<char style="ord">i</char> female servant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Let not my lord, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, regard this man of Belial <char style="add">[Worthless, Good for Nothing]</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char>: for as his name <char style="add">[is]</char>, so <char style="add">[is]</char> he; Naval <char style="add">[fool] [is]</char> his name, and folly <char style="add">[is]</char> with him: but I you<char style="ord">i</char> female servant saw not the young men of my lord, whom you<char style="ord">i</char> did send.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Now therefore, my lord, <char style="add">[as]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, and <char style="add">[as]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> soul lives, seeing the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has withheld you<char style="ord">i</char> from coming to <char style="add">[shed]</char> blood, and from avenging yourself with your<char style="ord">i</char> own hand, now let your<char style="ord">i</char> enemies, and they that seek evil to my lord, be as Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And now this blessing which you<char style="ord">i</char> female servant has brought unto my lord, let it even be given unto the young men that follow my lord.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, forgive the trespass of your<char style="ord">i</char> female servant: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will certainly make my lord a sure house; because my lord fights the battles of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and evil has not been found in you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[all]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Yet a man is risen to pursue you<char style="ord">i</char>, and to seek your<char style="ord">i</char> soul: but the soul of my lord shall be bound in the bundle of life with the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; and the souls of your<char style="ord">i</char> enemies, them shall he sling out, <char style="add">[as out]</char> of the middle of a sling.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, when the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall have done to my lord according to all the good that he has spoken concerning you<char style="ord">i</char>, and shall have appointed you<char style="ord">i</char> ruler over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />That this shall be no grief unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, nor offence of heart unto my lord, either that you<char style="ord">i</char> have shed blood causeless, or that my lord has avenged himself: but when the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall have dealt well with my lord, then remember you<char style="ord">i</char> female servant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said to Avigayil <char style="add">[my father is joy]</char>, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which sent you<char style="ord">i</char> this day to meet me:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> advice, and Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, which have kept me this day from coming to <char style="add">[shed]</char> blood, and from avenging myself with my own hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />For in very deed, <char style="add">[as]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> lives, which has kept me back from hurting you<char style="ord">i</char>, except you<char style="ord">i</char> had hasted and come to meet me, surely there had not been left unto Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char> by the morning light any that pisses against the wall.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> received of her hand <char style="add">[that]</char> which she had brought him, and said unto her, Go up in peace to you<char style="ord">i</char> house; see, I have listened to you<char style="ord">i</char> voice, and have accepted you<char style="ord">i</char> person.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And Avigayil <char style="add">[my father is joy]</char> came to Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char>; and, behold, he held a feast in his house, like the feast of a king; and Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char>’s heart <char style="add">[was]</char> merry within him, for he <char style="add">[was]</char> very drunken: wherefore she told him nothing, less or more, until the morning light.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />But it came to pass in the morning, when the wine was gone out of Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char>, and his wife had told him these things, that his heart died within him, and he became <char style="add">[as]</char> a stone.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And it came to pass about ten days <char style="add">[after]</char>, that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> struck Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char>, that he died.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And when David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> heard that Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char> was dead, he said, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that has pleaded the cause of my reproach <char style="pn">(disgrace; shame)</char> from the hand of Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char>, and has kept his servant from evil: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has returned the wickedness of Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char> upon his own head. And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> sent and communed with Avigayil <char style="add">[my father is joy]</char>, to take her to him to wife.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />And when the servants of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> were come to Avigayil <char style="add">[my father is joy]</char> to Carmel <char style="add">[Garden-land]</char>, they spoke unto her, saying, David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> sent us unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, to take you<char style="ord">i</char> to him to wife.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />And she arose, and bowed herself on <char style="add">[her]</char> face to the earth, and said, Behold, <char style="add">[let]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> female servant <char style="add">[be]</char> a servant to wash the feet of the servants of my lord.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />And Avigayil <char style="add">[my father is joy]</char> hasted, and arose, and rode upon an ass, with five female servants of hers that went after her; and she went after the messengers of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and became his wife.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> also took Achino’am <char style="add">[my brother is delight]</char> of Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>; and they were also both of them his wives.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />But Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> had given Mikhal <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> his daughter, David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s wife, to Palti <char style="add">[my deliverance]</char> the son of Layish <char style="add">[Lion]</char>, which <char style="add">[was]</char> of Gallim <char style="add">[springs]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="26" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the Zifim <char style="add">[smelters]</char> came unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> to Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, saying, Does not David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> hide himself in the hill of Hikhilah <char style="add">[dark]</char>, <char style="add">[which is]</char> before Y’shim’on <char style="add">[Wasteland]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Then Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> arose, and went down to the wilderness of Ziv <char style="add">[brightness] [Battlement (low wall around a roof; wall for defense)]</char>, having three thousand chosen men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> with him, to seek David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> in the wilderness of Ziv <char style="add">[brightness] [Battlement (low wall around a roof; wall for defense)]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> pitched in the hill of Hikhilah <char style="add">[dark]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> before Y’shim’on <char style="add">[Wasteland]</char>, by the way. But David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> abode in the wilderness, and he saw that Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> came after him into the wilderness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> therefore sent out spies, and understood that Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> was come in very deed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> arose, and came to the place where Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> had pitched: and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> beheld the place where Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> lay, and Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> the son of Ner <char style="add">[lamp]</char>, the captain of his host: and Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> lay in the trench, and the people pitched round about him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Then answered David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and said to Achi-Melekh <char style="add">[my brother is king]</char> the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>, and to Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char> the son of Tz’ruyah <char style="add">[balsam]</char>, brother to Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, saying, Who will go down with me to Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> to the camp? And Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char> said, I will go down with you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char> came to the people by night: and, behold, Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> lay sleeping within the trench, and his spear stuck in the ground at his bolster <char style="pn">(pillow; head - or other - support)</char>: but Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> and the people lay round about him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then said Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char> to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> has delivered you<char style="ord">i</char> enemy into you<char style="ord">i</char> hand this day: now therefore let me strike him, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, with the spear even to the earth at once, and I will not <char style="add">[strike]</char> him the second time.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said to Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char>, Destroy him not: for who can stretch forth his hand against the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> anointed, and be guiltless?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said furthermore, <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall strike him; or his day shall come to die; or he shall descend into battle, and perish.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> forbid that I should stretch forth my hand against the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> anointed: but, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, take you<char style="ord">i</char> now the spear that <char style="add">[is]</char> at his bolster <char style="pn">(pillow; head - or other - support)</char>, and the pot of water, and let us go.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> took the spear and the pot of water from Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> bolster <char style="add">(pillow; head - or other - support)</char>; and they got them away, and no man saw <char style="add">[it]</char>, nor knew <char style="add">[it]</char>, neither awakened: for they <char style="add">[were]</char> all asleep; because a deep sleep from the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was fallen upon them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Then David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> went over to the other side, and stood on the top of an hill afar off; a great space <char style="add">[being]</char> between them:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> cried to the people, and to Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> the son of Ner <char style="add">[lamp]</char>, saying, Answer you<char style="ord">i</char> not, Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char>? Then Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> answered and said, Who <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[that]</char> cries to the king?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said to Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char>, <char style="add">[Are]</char> not you<char style="ord">i</char> a <char style="add">[valiant]</char> man? and who <char style="add">[is]</char> like to you<char style="ord">i</char> in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>? wherefore then have you<char style="ord">i</char> not kept you<char style="ord">i</char> lord the king? for there came one of the people in to destroy the king you<char style="ord">i</char> lord.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />This thing <char style="add">[is]</char> not good that you<char style="ord">i</char> have done. <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, you<char style="ord">2f</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> worthy to die, because you<char style="ord">2f</char> have not kept your master, the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> anointed. And now see where the king’s spear <char style="add">[is]</char>, and the pot of water that <char style="add">[was]</char> at his bolster <char style="pn">(pillow; head - or other - support)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> knew David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s voice, and said, <char style="add">[Is]</char> this you<char style="ord">i</char> voice, my son David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>? And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said, <char style="add">[It is]</char> my voice, my lord, O king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And he said, For what reason does my lord thus pursue after his servant? for what have I done? or what evil <char style="add">[is]</char> in my hand?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Now therefore, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, let my lord the king hear the words of his servant. If the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have stirred you<char style="ord">i</char> up against me, let him accept an offering: but if <char style="add">[they be]</char> the children of men, cursed <char style="add">[be]</char> they before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; for they have driven me out this day from abiding in the inheritance of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, Go, serve other gods.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Now therefore, let not my blood fall to <char style="pn">(to do entirely, do wholly)</char> the earth before the face of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: for the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> is come out to seek a flea, as when one does hunt a partridge in the mountains.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Then said Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, I have sinned: return, my son David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: for I will no more do you<char style="ord">i</char> harm, because my soul was precious in your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes this day: behold, I have played the fool, and have erred exceedingly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> answered and said, Behold the king’s spear! and let one of the young men come over and fetch it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> render to every man his righteousness and his faithfulness: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> delivered you<char style="ord">i</char> into <char style="add">[my]</char> hand to day, but I would not stretch forth my hand against the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> anointed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And, behold, as your<char style="ord">i</char> life was much set by this day in my eyes, so let my life be much set by in the eyes of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and let him deliver me out of all tribulation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Then Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> said to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, my son David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: you<char style="ord">i</char> shall both do great <char style="add">[things]</char>, and also shall still prevail. So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> went on his way, and Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> returned to his place.</para>
  <chapter number="27" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said in his heart, I shall now perish one day by the hand of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>: <char style="add">[there is]</char> nothing better for me than that I should speedily escape into the land of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>; and Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> shall despair of me, to seek me any more in any coast of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: so shall I escape out of his hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> arose, and he passed over with the six hundred men that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him unto Akhish [meaning disputed; I will blacken <char style="pn">(or terrify)</char> or only a man], the son of Ma’okh <char style="add">[oppression]</char>, king of Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> dwelt with Akhish [meaning disputed; I will blacken <char style="pn">(or terrify)</char> or only a man] at Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>, he and his men, every man with his household, <char style="add">[even]</char> David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> with his two wives, Achino’am <char style="add">[my brother is delight]</char> the Yizre’elit <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>, and Avigayil <char style="add">[my father is joy]</char> the Carmelit <char style="add">[garden-land]</char>, Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char>’s wife.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And it was told Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> was fled to Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>: and he sought no more again for him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto Akhish <char style="add">[meaning disputed; I will blacken (or terrify) or only a man]</char>, If I have now found grace in you<char style="ord">i</char> eyes, let them give me a place in some town in the country, that I may dwell there: for why should you<char style="ord">i</char> servant dwell in the royal city with you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Then Akhish [meaning disputed; I will blacken <char style="pn">(or terrify)</char> or only a man] gave him Ziklag <char style="add">[Winding]</char> that day: wherefore Ziklag <char style="add">[Winding]</char> pertains unto the kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the time that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> dwelt in the country of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> was a full year and four months.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and his men went up, and invaded the G’shuri <char style="add">[A Bridge]</char>, and the Gizri <char style="add">[bridge]</char>, and the ‘Amalekim <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char>: for those <char style="add">[nations were]</char> of old the inhabitants of the land, as you<char style="ord">i</char> go to Shur <char style="add">[wall]</char>, even unto the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> struck the land, and left neither man nor woman alive, and took away the sheep, and the oxen, and the asses, and the camels, and the apparel, and returned, and came to Akhish <char style="add">[meaning disputed; I will blacken (or terrify) or only a man]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Akhish <char style="add">[meaning disputed; I will blacken (or terrify) or only a man]</char> said, Where have you<char style="ord">2f</char> made a raid to day? And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said, Against the south of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and against the south of the Yerachme’eli <char style="add">[my God have pity]</char>, and against the south of the Keini <char style="add">[traveling tinkers or blacksmiths]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> saved neither man nor woman alive, to bring <char style="add">[tidings]</char> to Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>, saying, Lest they should tell on us, saying, So did David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and so <char style="add">[will be]</char> his manner all the while he dwells in the country of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Akhish [meaning disputed; I will blacken <char style="pn">(or terrify)</char> or only a man] believed David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, saying, He has made his people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> utterly to abhor him; therefore he shall be my servant forever.</para>
  <chapter number="28" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass in those days, that the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> gathered their armies together for warfare, to fight with Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>. And Akhish [meaning disputed; I will blacken <char style="pn">(or terrify)</char> or only a man] said unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Know you<char style="ord">i</char> assuredly, that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall go out with me to battle, you<char style="ord">i</char> and you<char style="ord">i</char> men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said to Akhish <char style="add">[meaning disputed; I will blacken (or terrify) or only a man]</char>, Surely you<char style="ord">i</char> shall know what you<char style="ord">i</char> servant can do. And Akhish [meaning disputed; I will blacken <char style="pn">(or terrify)</char> or only a man] said to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Therefore will I make you<char style="ord">i</char> keeper of my head forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Now Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> was dead, and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> had lamented him, and buried him in Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, even in his own city. And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> had put away those that had familiar spirits, and the wizards, out of the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> gathered themselves together, and came and pitched in Shunem <char style="add">[Double Resting Place]</char>: and Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> gathered all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> together, and they pitched in Gilboa <char style="add">[swollen heap]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And when Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> saw the host of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, he was afraid, and his heart greatly trembled.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And when Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> enquired of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> answered him not, neither by dreams, nor by Urim <char style="add">[Lights]</char>, nor by prophets.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Then said Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> unto his servants, Seek me a woman that has a familiar spirit, that I may go to her, and enquire of her. And his servants said to him, Behold, <char style="add">[there is]</char> a woman that has a familiar spirit at ‘Ein-Dor <char style="add">[spring of dwelling]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And ha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> disguised himself, and put on other clothing, and he went, and two men with him, and they came to the woman by night: and he said, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, divine unto me by the familiar spirit, and bring me <char style="add">[him]</char> up, whom I shall name unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the woman said unto him, Behold, you<char style="ord">i</char> know what Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> has done, how he has cut off those that have familiar spirits, and the wizards, out of the land: wherefore then lay you<char style="ord">i</char> a snare for my life, to cause me to die?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> swore to her by the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, there shall no punishment happen to you<char style="ord">i</char> for this thing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Then said the woman, Whom shall I bring up unto you<char style="ord">i</char>? And he said, Bring me up Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And when the woman saw Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, she cried with a loud voice: and the woman spoke to Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, saying, Why have you<char style="ord">i</char> deceived me? for you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the king said unto her, Be not afraid: for what saw you<char style="ord">i</char>? And the woman said unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, I saw gods ascending out of the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he said unto her, What form <char style="add">[is]</char> he of? And she said, An old man comes up; and he <char style="add">[is]</char> covered with a Mantle <char style="pn">(cloak; covering garment)</char> <char style="pn">(cloak)</char>. And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> perceived that it <char style="add">[was]</char> Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, and he stooped with <char style="add">[his]</char> face to the ground, and bowed himself.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> said to Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, Why have you<char style="ord">i</char> disquieted me, to bring me up? And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> answered, I am sore distressed; for the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> make war against me, and God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> is departed from me, and answer me no more, neither by prophets, nor by dreams: therefore I have called you<char style="ord">i</char>, that you<char style="ord">i</char> may make known unto me what I shall do.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Then said Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>, For what reason then do you<char style="ord">i</char> ask of me, seeing the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> is departed from you<char style="ord">i</char>, and is become your<char style="ord">i</char> enemy?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has done to him, as he spoke by me: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has rent the kingdom out of your<char style="ord">i</char> hand, and given it to your<char style="ord">i</char> neighbour, <char style="add">[even]</char> to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Because you<char style="ord">i</char> obeyed not the voice of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, nor executed his fierce wrath upon ‘Amalek <char style="add">[Dweller in a Valley]</char>, therefore has the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> done this thing unto you<char style="ord">i</char> this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Moreover the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will also deliver Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char> into the hand of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>: and tomorrow <char style="add">[shall]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> and you<char style="ord">i</char> sons <char style="add">[be]</char> with me: the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> also shall deliver the host of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> into the hand of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Then Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> fell immediately all along on the earth, and was sore afraid, because of the words of Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char>: and there was no strength in him; for he had eaten no bread all the day, nor all the night.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the woman came unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and saw that he was sore troubled, and said unto him, Behold, your<char style="ord">i</char> female servant has obeyed your<char style="ord">i</char> voice, and I have put my life in my hand, and have listened unto your<char style="ord">i</char> words which you<char style="ord">i</char> spoke unto me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Now therefore, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, hearken you<char style="ord">i</char> also unto the voice of your<char style="ord">i</char> female servant, and let me set a morsel of bread before you<char style="ord">i</char>; and eat, that you<char style="ord">i</char> may have strength, when you<char style="ord">i</char> go on you<char style="ord">i</char> way.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />But he refused, and said, I will not eat. But his servants, together with the woman, compelled him; and he listened unto their voice. So he arose from the earth, and sat upon the bed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the woman had a fat calf in the house; and she hasted, and killed it, and took flour, and kneaded <char style="add">[it]</char>, and did bake unleavened bread thereof:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And she brought <char style="add">[it]</char> before Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and before his servants; and they did eat. Then they rose up, and went away that night.</para>
  <chapter number="29" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> gathered together all their armies to Aphek <char style="add">[Enclosure]</char>: and the Yisra’eli’s pitched by a fountain which <char style="add">[is]</char> in Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the lords of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> passed on by hundreds, and by thousands: but David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and his men passed on in the rear guard with Akhish <char style="add">[meaning disputed; I will blacken (or terrify) or only a man]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Then said the princes of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, What <char style="add">[do]</char> these ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew] [here]</char>? And Akhish [meaning disputed; I will blacken <char style="pn">(or terrify)</char> or only a man] said unto the princes of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, <char style="add">[Is]</char> not this David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, the servant of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which has been with me these days, or these years, and I have found no fault in him since he fell <char style="add">[unto me]</char> unto this day?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the princes of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> were exceedingly angry with him; and the princes of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> said unto him, Make this fellow return, that he may go again to his place which you<char style="ord">i</char> have appointed him, and let him not go down with us to battle, lest in the battle he be an adversary to us: for which should he reconcile himself unto his master? <char style="add">[should it]</char> not <char style="add">[be]</char> with the heads of these men?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Is]</char> not this David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, of whom they sang one to another in dances, saying, Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> killed his thousands, and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his ten thousands?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Then Akhish <char style="add">[meaning disputed; I will blacken (or terrify) or only a man]</char> called David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and said unto him, Surely, <char style="add">[as]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, you<char style="ord">i</char> have been upright, and you<char style="ord">i</char> going out and you<char style="ord">i</char> coming in with me in the host <char style="add">[is]</char> good in my sight: for I have not found evil in you<char style="ord">i</char> since the day of you<char style="ord">i</char> coming unto me unto this day: nevertheless the lords favour you<char style="ord">i</char> not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />For what reason now return, and go in peace, that you<char style="ord">i</char> displease not the lords of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto Akhish [meaning disputed; I will blacken <char style="pn">(or terrify)</char> or only a man], But what have I done? and what have you<char style="ord">i</char> found in your<char style="ord">i</char> servant so long as I have been with you<char style="ord">i</char> unto this day, that I may not go fight against the enemies of my lord the king?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Akhish [meaning disputed; I will blacken <char style="pn">(or terrify)</char> or only a man] answered and said to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, I know that you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> good in my sight, as an angel of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: notwithstanding the princes of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> have said, He shall not go up with us to the battle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />For what reason now rise up early in the morning with you<char style="ord">i</char> master’s servants that are come with you<char style="ord">i</char>: and as soon as you<char style="ord">2f</char> be up early in the morning, and have light, depart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and his men rose up early to depart in the morning, to return into the land of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>. And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> went up to Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="30" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass, when David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and his men were come to Ziklag <char style="add">[Winding]</char> on the third day, that the ‘Amalekim <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char> had invaded the south, and Ziklag <char style="add">[Winding]</char>, and smitten Ziklag <char style="add">[Winding]</char>, and burned it with fire;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And had taken the women captives, that <char style="add">[were]</char> in it: they killed not any, either great or small, but carried <char style="add">[them]</char> away, and went on their way.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and his men came to the city, and, behold, <char style="add">[it was]</char> burned with fire; and their wives, and their sons, and their daughters, were taken captives.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him lifted up their voice and wept, until they had no more power to weep.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s two wives were taken captives, Achino’am <char style="add">[my brother is delight]</char> the Yizre’elit <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>, and Avigayil <char style="add">[my father is joy]</char> the wife of Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char> the Carmeli <char style="add">[garden-land]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> was greatly distressed; for the people spoke of stoning him, because the soul of all the people was grieved, every man for his sons and for his daughters: but David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> encouraged himself in the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said to Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char> the priest, Achi-Melekh <char style="add">[my brother is king]</char>’s son, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, bring me here the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>. And Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char> brought there the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char> to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> enquired at the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, Shall I pursue after this troop? shall I overtake them? And he answered him, Pursue: for you<char style="ord">i</char> shall surely overtake <char style="add">[them]</char>, and without fail recover <char style="add">[all]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> went, he and the six hundred men that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him, and came to the brook B’sor <char style="add">[cheerful]</char>, where those that were left behind detained <char style="pn">(held)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />But David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> pursued, he and four hundred men: for two hundred abode behind, which were so faint that they could not go over the brook B’sor <char style="add">[cheerful]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And they found an Mitzri <char style="add">[Egyptian]</char> in the field, and brought him to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and gave him bread, and he did eat; and they made him drink water;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And they gave him a piece of a cake of figs, and two clusters of raisins: and when he had eaten, his spirit came again to him: for he had eaten no bread, nor drunk <char style="add">[any]</char> water, three days and three nights.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto him, To whom <char style="add">[belong]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>? and from what place <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>? And he said, I <char style="add">[am]</char> a young man of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, servant to an ‘Amaleki <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char>; and my master left me, because three days ago I fell sick.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />We made an invasion <char style="add">[upon]</char> the south of the K’reti <char style="add">[executioners]</char>, and upon <char style="add">[the coast]</char> which <char style="add">[belongs]</char> to Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and upon the south of Kalev <char style="add">[Dog]</char>; and we burned Ziklag <char style="add">[Winding]</char> with fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said to him, Can you<char style="ord">i</char> bring me down to this company? And he said, Swear unto me by God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, that you<char style="ord">i</char> will neither kill me, nor deliver me into the hands of my master, and I will bring you<char style="ord">i</char> down to this company.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And when he had brought him down, behold, <char style="add">[they were]</char> spread abroad upon all the earth, eating and drinking, and dancing, because of all the great spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> that they had taken out of the land of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and out of the land of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> struck them from the twilight even unto the evening of the next day: and there escaped not a man of them, save four hundred young men, which rode upon camels, and fled.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> recovered all that the ‘Amalekim <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char> had carried away: and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> rescued his two wives.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And there was nothing lacking to them, neither small nor great, neither sons nor daughters, neither spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>, nor any <char style="add">[thing]</char> that they had taken to them: David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> recovered all.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> took all the flocks and the herds, <char style="add">[which]</char> they drove before those <char style="add">[other]</char> cattle, and said, This <char style="add">[is]</char> David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> came to the two hundred men, which were so faint that they could not follow David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, whom they had made also to abide at the brook B’sor <char style="add">[cheerful]</char>: and they went forth to meet David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and to meet the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him: and when David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> came near to the people, he saluted them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Then answered all the wicked men and <char style="add">[men]</char> of Belial <char style="add">[Worthless, Good for Nothing]</char>, of those that went with David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and said, Because they went not with us, we will not give them <char style="add">[ought]</char> of the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> that we have recovered, save to every man his wife and his children, that they may lead <char style="add">[them]</char> away, and depart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Then said David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not do so, my brethren, with that which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has given us, who has preserved us, and delivered the company that came against us into our hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />For who will hearken unto you in this matter? but as his part <char style="add">[is]</char> that goes down to the battle, so <char style="add">[shall]</char> his part <char style="add">[be]</char> that tarries by the stuff: they shall part alike.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And it was <char style="add">[so]</char> from that day forward, that he made it a statute and an ordinance for Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And when David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> came to Ziklag <char style="add">[Winding]</char>, he sent of the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> unto the elders of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> to his friends, saying, Behold a present for you of the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> of the enemies of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />To <char style="add">[them]</char> which <char style="add">[were]</char> in Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>, and to <char style="add">[them]</char> which <char style="add">[were]</char> in south Ramot <char style="add">[Heights]</char>, and to <char style="add">[them]</char> which <char style="add">[were]</char> in Yatir <char style="add">[Plenty]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And to <char style="add">[them]</char> which <char style="add">[were]</char> in ‘Aeo’er <char style="add">[Ruins]</char>, and to <char style="add">[them]</char> which <char style="add">[were]</char> in Sifmot <char style="add">[fruitful]</char>, and to <char style="add">[them]</char> which <char style="add">[were]</char> in Esht’moa <char style="add">[I will make myself heard]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And to <char style="add">[them]</char> which <char style="add">[were]</char> in Rakhal <char style="add">[trade]</char>, and to <char style="add">[them]</char> which <char style="add">[were]</char> in the cities of the Yerachme’eli <char style="add">[my God have pity]</char>, and to <char style="add">[them]</char> which <char style="add">[were]</char> in the cities of the Keini <char style="add">[traveling tinkers or blacksmiths]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And to <char style="add">[them]</char> which <char style="add">[were]</char> in Hormah <char style="add">[Asylum]</char>, and to <char style="add">[them]</char> which <char style="add">[were]</char> in Kor-’Ashan <char style="add">[furnace of smoke]</char>, and to <char style="add">[them]</char> which <char style="add">[were]</char> in ‘Atakh <char style="add">[lodging place]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And to <char style="add">[them]</char> which <char style="add">[were]</char> in Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>, and to all the places where David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> himself and his men were wont <char style="pn">(used to; in the habit of)</char> to haunt <char style="pn">(where one goes freequently)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="31" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> fought against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> fled from before the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and fell down slain in mount Gilboa <char style="add">[swollen heap]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> followed hard upon Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and upon his sons; and the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> killed Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>, and Avinadav <char style="add">[my father is noble]</char>, and Malkishua <char style="add">[my king is wealth]</char>, Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> sons.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the battle went sore against Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and the archers hit him; and he was sore wounded of the archers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then said Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> unto his armourbearer, Draw your<char style="ord">i</char> sword, and thrust me through with that; lest these uncircumcised come and thrust me through, and abuse me. But his armourbearer would not; for he was sore afraid. Therefore Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> took a sword, and fell upon it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And when his armourbearer saw that Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> was dead, he fell likewise upon his sword, and died with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />So Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> died, and his three sons, and his armourbearer, and all his men, that same day together.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And when the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that <char style="add">[were]</char> on the other side of the valley, and <char style="add">[they]</char> that <char style="add">[were]</char> on the other side Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>, saw that the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> fled, and that Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and his sons were dead, they forsook the cities, and fled; and the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> came and dwelt in them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And it came to pass on the morrow, when the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> came to strip the slain, that they found Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and his three sons fallen in mount Gilboa <char style="add">[swollen heap]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And they cut off his head, and stripped off his armour, and sent into the land of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> round about, to publish <char style="add">[it in]</char> the house of their idols, and among the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And they put his armour in the house of ‘Ashtarot <char style="add">[Star (female deity)]</char>: and they fastened his body to the wall of Beit-Sh’an <char style="add">[house of ease]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And when the inhabitants of Yavesh-Gil’ad <char style="add">[Dry Hill of Testimony]</char> heard of that which the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> had done to Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />All the valiant men arose, and went all night, and took the body of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and the bodies of his sons from the wall of Beit-Sh’an <char style="add">[house of ease]</char>, and came to Yavesh <char style="add">[dry]</char>, and burnt them there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And they took their bones, and buried <char style="add">[them]</char> under a tree at Yavesh <char style="add">[dry]</char>, and fasted seven days.</para>
</usx>